in-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T18:03:42-07:00","id":1506099,"title":"","content":"Okay, one more time, I think we can't Scrutinize twice if we already got something on the Scrutiny, so I think we can continue:<br /> <br /> Gnosis (1) + Prime (2) + coin bonus (1) + teamwork bonus (1) + Opacity (-1), 4 dice with 8-again<br /> <br /> [<b>10</b>, <b>9</b>, 7, 7, <b>8</b>, 5, 4]<br /> <br /> 3 successes, we are good to go","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T18:46:14-07:00","id":1506101,"title":"","content":"Surface/Deep Information<ul><li>A Space spell of the Shielding Practice.</li> <li>It seems to be a barrier - the cobalt-blue sheen it creates on the wall gives off the impression of a lensing effect, stolidly rejecting any scrap of Space-aspected Arcana that comes near it.</li> <li>The Nimbus is too faded to fully detect, but there is a faint sensation of cold hands latching onto your wrists and legs.</li> <li>Spell Factors are primarily sunk into Duration and Scale, encapsulating the room. It has been active for <i>many</i> years, and is almost as old as the house. It is relinquished, and at Indefinite Duration. The method of relinquishment feels... odd, though this impression is strongest when viewed under Elpis' Mind-enhanced scrutiny. The &quot;knot&quot; that ties it off vibrates slightly, as if screaming. (Relinquishment method is another Mystery, Opacity 2. You players can probably guess what it is pretty easily though.)</li> <li>There seems to be another spell ongoing just &quot;behind&quot; the barrier - a Ruling Prime spell of some kind, set along the same boundaries but within the room. If the Shielding is set along the outside of the room, then this Prime spell is likely set up inside the room like wallpaper.</li> </ul>\u200bEdit: Also, gain another regular Beat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T18:58:40-07:00","id":1506103,"title":"","content":"Huh\u2026an actual Ward? Seems the best bet for the Space Shielding.<br /> Elpis definitely won\u2019t think of it immediately, but I\u2019m pretty sure that was relinquished by the trauma method. Yaaaaay. <br /> I\u2019m going to assume Elpis doesn\u2019t recognize the nimbus, planning on examining it later.<br /> The Prime Ruling behind it is definitely interesting though. Maybe it\u2019s another barrier? To keep resonance and/or the nimbus from spilling out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T20:50:56-07:00","id":1506112,"title":"","content":"Uh, is the nimbus of a person kept current to the how they are, or is the nimbus preserved as it was at the time of casting? Should I roll for Elpis to know that?<br /> <br /> Edit: clarity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-22-2023, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-21T21:21:40-07:00","id":1506114,"title":"","content":"I don't think it's clarified in RAW, so I go with the Nimbus of a Relinquished spell reflecting the Nimbus the Mage had at the time. One still being maintained would continue to adapt along with the owner, albeit on a slight delay.<br /> <br /> Given Elpis' background, there's no problem with them knowing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T10:33:18-07:00","id":1506152,"title":"","content":"Just so y\u2019all are clear, the progression of Elpis thoughts were: sees evidence that someone did something rather upsetting, gets upset, asks if the people ended up damaging themselves to the point that they had lost free will, and then tries to draw a silver lining from this that ties into their beliefs about the world. I don\u2019t know if that was clear, had a lot of rewrites. <br /> <br /> Should that have been mostly internal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T11:30:46-07:00","id":1506155,"title":"","content":"Only one part didn't come through: &quot;asks if the people ended up damaging themselves to the point that they had lost free will&quot;. Which given that the method used was likely Broken Relinquishment, it less likely free will was lost, rather sanity and mental wellness.<br /> <br /> Roleplay wise, I think it was spot on, a strong reaction to having the situation press on an open wound and then trying to grasp onto higher ideals.<br /> <br /> There is some projecting onto the unknown situation, but it feels right for a very emotional response. What makes me really curious is how Elpis will react to a Guardian in a moment of &quot;Sins for a just end grant Wisdom&quot; or an Arrow having no choice but to kill. Will they have enough of a filter to accept that or will it trigger their internal alarm ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T12:08:23-07:00","id":1506158,"title":"","content":"\u2026.from their point of view Rapture is loosing the ability to choose anything but to purse their fault. That\u2019s why Elpis was asking about Rapture. It\u2019s not the whole story, of course, but they have been looking into Rapture, and most records of the Rapt aren\u2019t going have the Nameless and Accursed mechanics along side it. <br /> <br /> Elpis would probably bitterly argue against the Gaurdian trying &quot;Sins for a just end grant Wisdom&quot; on them\u2026right now. The ends justify the means as a philosophy just doesn\u2019t sit well with them. Part of their problem is arguing from a place of Ideals, without taking into account the real. I expect character development when we eventually figure out what happened to Pandora.<br /> <br /> An Arrow has a much higher chance of successfully arguing the necessity of killing someone to Elpis. Magic is uniquely powerful, and can be creatively used to avoid killing, and stunning spells are much easier than killing spells. However, combat is combat, and people have to make decisions in moments about who lives and who dies. Unlike a Guardian, an Arrow isn\u2019t completely arguing the ends completely justify the means. They are usually pointing out in combat situations, sometimes someone can\u2019t be safely talked down, or safely incapacitated without risking the lives of others. Basically, they force Elpis to consider reality alongside their ideals with these scenarios. In the end, this isn\u2019t really that different an argument from the Guardians but it\u2019s one Elpis could accept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T12:53:06-07:00","id":1506166,"title":"","content":"To clarify further, Elpis is running off a White Council from the Dresden Files morality aka certain acts damage the self along with damaging others, which in Awakening terms is Wisdom and Rapture. They are currently conflating Morality with Wisdom, due to their understanding of the nature of Rapture. One of the reasons they\u2019re suspicious of Pandora\u2019s Rapture is that she wasn\u2019t a bad person. Not perfect, sure, but very kind and caring. And what they saw of her Nimbus backed that up. I\u2019m hoping part of their development is coming to the understanding that Wisdom is more like Sanity than Morality, and working from there.<br /> <br /> Edit: Elpis thinks that Guardians are just flat out wrong about \u201cSins for a just end bring Wisdom\u201d.Right now they think that the Guardians and the Arrow are just resilient to Wisdom loss. It\u2019s going to be quite the moment when they find out that a Guardian actually gained Wisdom for assassinating someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-22-2023, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T18:18:52-07:00","id":1506195,"title":"","content":"Hey, I just wanted to say I\u2019ve been having lots of fun so far! The cottage has been very cool, with all of the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> Anyways\u2026that at least looks like a legacy summoning circle, made with large amounts of safety in mind. Given the description of the legacy, I can\u2019t imagine anything they summoned would be nice and friendly, so the protection seems warranted. Maybe the scratches on the wall from something they summoned? Definitely giving off a lot of bad vibes, which I\u2019m sure the resonance will reflect.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> what do you think, now that we\u2019ve seen the the major notes of the house?\u200b<br /> <br /> Definitely needs slightly more investigation of this last room, but I think we\u2019ve seen most of the major notes of the place. If we take it, Elpis is going to insist on a lot of redecorating/purification. Which it needed in the physical anyways, but also the supernatural stuff too. The trauma Ward is not currently within their current abilities to take down, but Elpis is definitely not happy with its current existence. It is useful, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T18:53:27-07:00","id":1506197,"title":"","content":"Same, I am having a blast.<br /> <br /> So its a binding circle ? Legacies can summon anywhere and not risk the summon being consumed by the Abyss, since they always return to the Supernal safely. So perhaps it wasn't for an Attainment, but for general research. Since they were Left-Handed, they could have confiscated any soul stones. Makes sense.<br /> <br /> Qaf is going to insist on fumigating the place, since he found rat droppings. But the Mind spell won't allow them to call someone, so hopefully a hardware store would have a way to do it yourself ? Deep cleaning, first aid kit, emergency rations, burn ointment (always have near the kitchen) and supplies for the fireplace (to harness mana) would be the basics. But yeah, refurbishing is the first order of business.<br /> <br /> Second order is probably cabal name, sigil and which Great Precepts we recognize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:05:47-07:00","id":1506199,"title":"","content":"Glad you're enjoying it! Don't hesitate to let me know if you need me to change anything<br /> <br /> Hyleen Cottage holds more Qaf-adjascent hooks than Njord's Draught does, and has more stationary plot-points. The Draught holds a few more Elpis-adjascent hooks, and has immediate access to otherwise fluid, political plot-points.<br /> <br /> Hyleen has also ended up much darker than I intended it - the initial Hallow list was just napkin-sketching, and I expanded on the ones you wanted to have a look at. Originally it was just a dilapidated old house, now it's the cenotaph and grave of a Left Handed Cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:27:34-07:00","id":1506201,"title":"","content":"One thing I wanted to confirm please. So Qaf is pretty practical by nature and has a backpack ready for mage work (discrete and helps ground Qafsiel's Shadow Name with travel symbolism), which is where he got the notebook from. Should I send a list of the things he carries for sanity checking ? Things like a notepad, canteen, notebook, duct tape, zip bags, swiss army knife, etc. In general terms, if anyone looked inside, it would seem like a few useful things for someone who goes hiking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:39:02-07:00","id":1506202,"title":"","content":"We can go one of two routes - <br /> 1. You can pull whatever you like out of the bag, but I have veto rights on if something is unreasonable<br /> <br /> 2. You keep a runing tally of what you're carrying<br /> <br /> I'm fine with either.<br /> <br /> The Invisible Runes constitute an Opacity 2 Mystery by the way, and work as an Enviroment Yantra for ritual spells of the Time, Space, or Mind Arcana that make use of the circles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:49:42-07:00","id":1506203,"title":"","content":"Well, I like how it's turned out so far! I was expecting a nice cheerful if slightly run-down sort of place. Instead, we found out it was a murder cult clubhouse. (Hopefully an exaggeration, but I know what type of universe Mage takes place in) <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/\">KaiserAfini</a> I think I can think of ways to allow Sleepers/Sleepwalkers to access the place for a job. I think the spell on it is more &quot;don't care about me&quot; rather than &quot;I don't exist&quot;, so there should be workarounds. Or we can ask some Changelings to do it through the Njord's Draught. I'm sure <i>nothing</i> can go wrong by favor trading with the fey.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:54:28-07:00","id":1506204,"title":"","content":"It's a &quot;not my problem&quot; field, so leading people through the boundry would bring them in without Dissonance. As long as, y'know, you haven't installed something that <i>should</i> be eye-catching, like a giant neon sign or a tree made of solid gold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:58:21-07:00","id":1506205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1506202#post1506202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We can go one of two routes -<br /> 1. You can pull whatever you like out of the bag, but I have veto rights on if something is unreasonable<br /> <br /> 2. You keep a runing tally of what you're carrying<br /> <br /> I'm fine with either.<br /> <br /> The Invisible Runes constitute an Opacity 2 Mystery by the way, and work as an Enviroment Yantra for ritual spells of the Time, Space, or Mind Arcana that make use of the circles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Unfortunately, I'm out of Willpower, so no dice pool boosting or scrutiny, so I'm rocking 2 dice for basic information (1 Gnosis + 2 Mind + 1 yantra -2 opacity). Not great odds, but hopefully not a dramatic failure risk? [8 8] = 2 success....the heck? Why can't you do this when I have dicepools of 6+?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T20:59:34-07:00","id":1506206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1506204#post1506204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a &quot;not my problem&quot; field, so leading people through the boundry would bring them in without Dissonance. As long as, y'know, you haven't installed something that <i>should</i> be eye-catching, like a giant neon sign or a tree made of solid gold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww...no angels dancing on the head of pin as lawn decoration. Dang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T21:02:08-07:00","id":1506207,"title":"","content":"Er, just so we're all clear, you don't <i>have</i> to solve all the Mysteries right now. Both Hyleen and the Draught are common property until/unless you claim them. Coming back is just a matter of getting permission from one of the Councilors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T21:06:50-07:00","id":1506208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1506207#post1506207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, just so we're all clear, you don't <i>have</i> to solve all the Mysteries right now. Both Hyleen and the Draught are common property until/unless you claim them. Coming back is just a matter of getting permission from one of the Councilors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops. Yeah ok, let's leave this for later.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T21:29:27-07:00","id":1506209,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a> Hey, how are you feeling on Vows? I'm considering Elpis to take up Honesty and Pacifism, not hard choices especially for them morally, but Pacifism depends on it being a dangerous environment, and Honesty might be a problem for us down the road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-22T22:22:00-07:00","id":1506212,"title":"","content":"Vows are good. I'll adapt as we go, but I have threats up to and including a Mage War, if we need it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T14:37:45-07:00","id":1506264,"title":"","content":"I think I will go with a tally, because that gives more room for him to be blindsided and challenge his adaptability as an Arrow, which feels more interesting. Okay, so the tentative list for his backpack:<ul><li>Notepad (for quick notes) and pens</li> <li>A change of clothes</li> <li>An insulated sports canteen filled with water</li> <li>Swiss army knife</li> <li>Notebook (for more detailed notes)</li> <li>Two sharpies, one of which is ultraviolet (for discrete runes)</li> <li>100 dollars in cash for emergencies</li> <li>Duct tape</li> <li>Cigarettes and zippo lighter. Qaf doesn't smoke, but one justifies the other and the cigarettes are good yantras for scrying and revelation</li> <li>Some paper clips and bobby pins</li> <li>A couple of ziploc bags</li> <li>A collapsible umbrella</li> <li>Micro USB and charger plug (in case he needs to recharge his phone)</li> <li>Nintendo switch with charger</li> <li>A flashlight with a toggle for LED mode and blacklight mode, with some replacement batteries</li> <li>UV safety glasses</li> </ul>On his person he has<ul><li>His wallet</li> <li>A handkerchief</li> <li>Some leather gloves in his coat pocket (good for the cold and examining weird stuff)</li> <li>His smartphone</li> <li>The watch that is his Dedicated Tool</li> <li>Car keys with the coin attached to the keychain</li> <li>House keys</li> </ul>Please let me know if this sounds ok, and if makes sense space wise and thematically, its supposed to be helpful everyday stuff people wouldn't bat an eye at seeing.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I just noticed I misread and the runes are not High Speech, I will make changes to my last IC post to correct it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"Kai