ilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T13:53:56-07:00","id":1507437,"title":"","content":"OK, we'll use a truncated version of a Krewe then. I'll ask that you OOC decide on:<br /> <br /> 1. Doctrine<br /> <br /> 2. Virtue and Creed<br /> <br /> 3. Attributes - Resistance will represent the Cabal's financial status and social standing. Finess and Power will stay roughly the same.<br /> <br /> 4. Merits - after claiming Hyleen Cottage, you have three dots you can spend. Doesn't have to be now. If you turn it into an actual Cult, we'll design a <i>Mystery Cult</i> merit for it.<br /> <br /> No Ceremonies, since you both basically <i>are</i> Ceremonies. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T14:42:38-07:00","id":1507438,"title":"","content":"I would also add name and sigil to the attributes, as well as which of the Great Rights we uphold.<br /> <br /> Not upholding the Right of Nemesis, for example, means we can go all out on enemies, but things will escalate easily. Upholding it means trying to first solve things with the Duel Arcane, which can be tough, and we cannot help anyone who recognizes it settle things privately.<br /> <br /> Recognizing the Right of Emeritus means we may get caught in the messes of the higher ups, but we eventually could wield that clout. Not recognizing it means a bit more work might be needed for them to commit their resources and so on.\u200b<br /> <br /> I am in favor of the Rights of Hospitality, Crossing and Sanctuary. Still thinking about Nemesis and Emeritus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-04-2023, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T18:31:47-07:00","id":1507444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1507438#post1507438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also add name and sigil to the attributes, as well as which of the Great Rights we uphold.<br /> <br /> Not upholding the Right of Nemesis, for example, means we can go all out on enemies, but things will escalate easily. Upholding it means trying to first solve things with the Duel Arcane, which can be tough, and we cannot help anyone who recognizes it settle things privately.<br /> <br /> Recognizing the Right of Emeritus means we may get caught in the messes of the higher ups, but we eventually could wield that clout. Not recognizing it means a bit more work might be needed for them to commit their resources and so on.\u200b<br /> <br /> I am in favor of the Rights of Hospitality, Crossing and Sanctuary. Still thinking about Nemesis and Emeritus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit confused as to what Emeritus actually means in practical terms. Does it mean that we are under the command of the Consilium? or that we listen when say...the Adamant Sage says maybe act defensively? Or is it that we give special privileges to those who have a certain Rank if they visit us?<br /> <br /> I think Nemesis is a mixed bag either way. Elpis would probably value least having the possibility of resolving things relatively peacefully, even with the conflict of others. So, a nay from them.<br /> <br /> As for our Virtue and Creed...I think our Creed should be something like Prudent. Qaf is focused on preparedness, and Elpis wants a better future, and I think that's a good adjective that includes both perspectives. Not sure what our Virtue should be.<br /> <br /> Doctrine is a bit too nebulous at the moment, though Elpis would like the idea of expanding the Right of Hospitality to include Changelings. I think that's a little impractical given our current situation though.<br /> <br /> Maybe we should have Gil and Jaye be allies with our merits?<br /> <br /> Attributes...I have no clue. We start with a Dot in each and have 6 more to distribute wherever...I usually favor Resistance attributes, but right now though I can't imagine we have much in the way of Money and Standing. I can see us earning a lot of goodwill, over time, but I think we need to do something first. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T18:43:21-07:00","id":1507447,"title":"","content":"So we have Elpis, the spirit of hope, the last being to emerge from Pandora's Box and possible child of Nyx. We also have Qafsiel, whose name means &quot;God is my speed&quot; or &quot;God is my cover&quot;, guardian of the seventh heaven, doom of kings and angel of time. What common themes and symbols do we have ? That could help us flesh out the principals of our Krewe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T18:50:04-07:00","id":1507449,"title":"","content":"My understanding of Emeritus is that you have to treat those with greater Gnosis/Arcana Mastery with more deference, whereas not taking Emeritus means you should listen, but don't have to obey. <br /> <br /> Jaye and Gil can either be dot(s) of Ally [The Draught], or separate dots of Ally [Court of Favors] and Ally [Court of Barter]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T20:17:56-07:00","id":1507452,"title":"","content":"I found more information:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Right of Emeritus</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Those who have earned respect must be treated with respect</b>. Traditionally, this refers to the practice of respecting one's elders. In practice, it's been broadened today to mean that those who have earned respect, must be respected. Respect is measured through word and deed. And that person's area of expertise should have a direct or substantial benefit to the cabal. Maybe they have a PhD in Mechanical Engineering or maybe they have a Black Belt in three different martial arts; in both cases, they should be given respect and deference within their area of expertise.<br /> <br /> Additionally, although not as widely practiced, is the giving of respect to those who have gained a certain position or title such as Councilor or Herald.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Right of Nemesis</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>When vengeance is declared, let none stand in its way</b>. Nemesis covers overt violence between mages. In other words, when a conflict is approved under the Precept of War, don't get in the middle of the feud. When it is invoked, then the cabal needs to be preparing for it as it stays in effect until the conflict is resolved. Additionally, no mage should interfere with the feud unless it becomes a direct threat to them. This is not a right that should be invoked lightly or with hubris.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Overview:</b></span><br /> <br /> Emeritus seems to mean, give authority due respect, deference and provide assistance when required. Treat others who have benefited the Consilia or cabal with equal respect. Seems pretty reasonable at a cursory glance.<br /> <br /> The key detail is that the Right of Nemesis can only be called after the Precept of War is declared by the Consilia. Which means it requires an attempt at mediation, if that fails a Duel Arcane might be called and if even that is insufficient, then Nemesis is publically notorized and all other mages who recognize the Right do not interfere in the feud. So what I interpreted from that is that it binds you to a system of sanity checks to prevent escalation, and even if it fails, it seeks to reduce the scale of the damage. If our goal is to resolve things peacefully or limit the damage we cause, this seems like the way to go. What do you think ?<br /> <br /> <br /> I am still pondering about the Krewe stats, but Prudent feels accurate.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T21:46:25-07:00","id":1507652,"title":"","content":"So, on common symbols and themes...I can't really tell off the bat. Elpis chose their shadow name to honor their mentor, to show what they believe is one of the most important things in life, what they want to grow into being, and eventually as a title to the concept they wish to ascend as. That isn't to say they want to be a hero, to be one whom people hope to save them. Rather, they wish to be that pale, ephemeral thing, that prolongs torment and refuses to let one accept the way life is. They know that things could have been different, that they could have lived a quiet and peaceful life. But that life was a life of despair, of knowing nothing would ever really change. They could never go back to that life. They aren't perfect, and they may be placing too much faith in the power of shadow names to shape one's nature, but they truly hope, and that keeps them going.<br /> <br /> Why did Qaf choose his name? Perhaps we can find common ground there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T08:53:06-07:00","id":1507693,"title":"","content":"Qafsiel chose his Shadow Name due to it embodying his view on magic. As far he knows, he was just running to achieve his goal, then he suddenly started running through Time and beyond that. Now he has magic and also signed up for the journey of a lifetime, so he might as well use the opportunity to leave things a bit better than when he started. But at the same time, the Awakening parsed magic as something that charged his hands and limbs, which left the impression that just like martial arts, it can do a lot of harm if he doesn't use it responsibly.<br /> <br /> The archangel Cassiel/Qafsiel embodies that perspective. He is the ruler of Saturn, whose symbolism is that of discipline, responsibility and ambition. He is the known as the archangel of Tears and Solitude, in the sense that he is with people on the lowest points of their life, telling them &quot;you CAN change things for the better&quot;. That symbolism of choosing to proactively seize hope, rather than have it delivered (you need to choose to act once you know there is a chance), resonates a lot with Qaf, and he is likely to stand with those that take that perspective, its why his Nimbus reflects it at all levels.<br /> <br /> <i>Observation:</i> Qafsiel also has the title of <i>The Death of Kings</i>, and during his Awakening, he was attacking dieselpunk Iron demons/robots. I don't think he has enough context yet to realize that picking that Shadow Name is probably making a statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-07-2023, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-07T16:26:02-07:00","id":1507716,"title":"","content":"So, I think it's clear hope can be our resonant symbol. Would it be accurate to say the Elpis focuses on Hope as a motivator, and Qaf focuses on what you do with Hope? That is to say, Elpis focuses on Hope as a Seed, the potential for growth, while Qaf focuses on growing that seed into a healthy and mighty tree?<br /> <br /> As for our sigil, Elpis uses Stars and Light as symbols for hope. I think Qaf uses the charge of the Storm and Lightning as symbols of hope? Could our sigil be a stylized version of this image? What do you think?<br /> <br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1188_1680909322858_636\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1188\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1188\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1188&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <i>Observation</i>: Wow, things sure seem to be setting up a lot of Kings who might be abusing their power, and might be in need of a good old punch. Hope no one has a Name that might make them nervous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-threa