o character summaries. Anything else I should know before making a character?<br /> <br /> Coincidentally, my last Mage Chronicle was set in Seattle. Weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T05:01:34-07:00","id":1511856,"title":"","content":"If you're not in a rush, I'd give the IC thread a skim","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T05:38:36-07:00","id":1511861,"title":"","content":"I think that, once CalvinSiler's character sheet and backstory are uploaded, it might be helpful for Cauthon to edit the first OOC comment to include links to character dossiers and setting information. That makes it much easier to keep track of who we know and have an overview of the political structure. The IC thread has it on the first post, but I think having it all in one index would be even more convenient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T06:01:23-07:00","id":1511863,"title":"","content":"Sounds good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T06:54:29-07:00","id":1511866,"title":"","content":"I'm about halfway through the IC thread. It seems like a Thyrsus or Moros would be most helpful to balancing out the cabal. Is that correct? Also, is there a gnosis 2 cap, and do you prefer a physically younger mage to keep with the theme of the Chronicle. <br /> <br /> Are there any character concepts that would be off limits?<br /> <br /> Just trying to get a sense of what the rules/guidelines are. I'm always interested in being helpful and a team player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T09:17:10-07:00","id":1511872,"title":"","content":"Thyrsus or Moros sound great. Right now only Elpis can pick up on the presence of goetia passively, being able to perceive more type of Ephemeral Entity would be very helpful.<br /> <br /> I don't think we discussed any limits, but we both started at Gnosis 1 and have gained 2 regular beats so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T09:39:57-07:00","id":1511876,"title":"","content":"OK. Finished skimming the IC thread. Moros could be interesting considering the conflict with White Sands. I was thinking it might be interesting to have a character who is interested in exploring the mystery of the cabal that used to occupy the cottage, maybe is even a descendent of one of the cabal. I forget if they were Silver Ladder or not. I see that you had contracts with the Changelings, but I thought it might also be interesting to have a mage who is interested in crafting and specializes in sanctum repair - sort of a This Old House/HGTV type.<br /> <br /> Other concepts I thought of were a student at the University, or a Guardian associated with the &quot;Factory&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or I've got even weirder ideas connected to my previous chronicle that was in Seattle, but I don't want to bleed too much of past games into whatever Cauthon has planned. <br /> <br /> BTW A Brotherhood of Demon WInd storyline sounds like a lot of fun. I think Elpis should go for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T09:39:57-07:00","id":1511877,"title":"","content":"OK. Finished skimming the IC thread. Moros could be interesting considering the conflict with White Sands. I was thinking it might be interesting to have a character who is interested in exploring the mystery of the cabal that used to occupy the cottage, maybe is even a descendent of one of the cabal. I forget if they were Silver Ladder or not. I see that you had contracts with the Changelings, but I thought it might also be interesting to have a mage who is interested in crafting and specializes in sanctum repair - sort of a This Old House/HGTV type.<br /> <br /> Other concepts I thought of were a student at the University, or a Guardian associated with the &quot;Factory&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or I've got even weirder ideas connected to my previous chronicle that was in Seattle, but I don't want to bleed too much of past games into whatever Cauthon has planned. <br /> <br /> BTW A Brotherhood of Demon WInd storyline sounds like a lot of fun. I think Elpis should go for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T11:05:38-07:00","id":1511888,"title":"","content":"Well, someone needs to know what exactly they replaced the wood with! Is hedge rock actually a recognizable stone type? Or just stone?<br /> <br /> That being said, play whatever you find fun. If we have 3 Obrimos, we could totally do crazy things with Forces and Prime. Same with Mastigos and Acanthus, and their respective Arcana. But if you are not really feeling a particular Path, yeah a Matter focused Moros is currently the spiciest option. <br /> <br /> (Did you mean Qaf? It might be a bit strange for a near pacifist to go into the Brotherhood.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T11:28:53-07:00","id":1511894,"title":"","content":"Oops. Yeah I meant Qaf. Qafsiel can mean &quot;Wrath of g'd&quot;.<br /> <br /> I dunno. I'm kind of digging the Thyrsus concept i have kicking around my head right now. But I could be persuaded towards Moros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T14:22:07-07:00","id":1511913,"title":"","content":"I think Af (anger) and Hemah (wrath) are the angels most associated with those themes, but I just double checked and it seems Qafsiel can have that meaning as well, that is pretty cool. Qafsiel's most known translation is &quot;Speed of God&quot;, which is why OOC I am aiming for him to join the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1494354-the-expeditious-explorers-an-obrimos-legacy-of-speedsters\">Expeditious Explorers</a>, which can be described as a mix of Indiana Jones and The Flash. However, he is not aware of them IC, which is why he will agree to meet the onikaze, since they are known to be great warriors. <br /> <br /> Another fun fact is that Qafsiel is also known as the death of kings, which will probably not make the Adamant Crown all too happy. <br /> <br /> Do you have an idea for the Moros ? I just checked, the previous owners of the Sanctum were a Ladder cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T14:55:01-07:00","id":1511918,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a Ladder Cabal from a few decades ago. I'd not recommend direct descent from them - an apprentice of one of their former apprentices would be fine, but any closer and they'd likely have been caught up in whatever Left-handed things the Cabal had been up to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:07:30-07:00","id":1511920,"title":"","content":"I was thinking of going with a balanced Silver Ladder Shaman: Life 2, Spirit 2, Matter 2<br /> <br /> Rotes: Persuasion Skill, Control Instincts (L2), Command Spirit (S2), Shaping (M2)<br /> Praxis: Speak with Beasts<br /> <br /> Asperations<br /> 1. Restore or Repair an area (on both sides of the gauntlet) that has fallen into disrepair.<br /> 2. Befriend a Forsaken Pack (at the ST's discretion of course)<br /> 3. Guide an awakening<br /> <br /> Obsession<br /> Uncover the Mystery of the Ruins of the Deep (i.e. why sleepers and not awakened, possible connection to Atlantis, etc.)<br /> <br /> I'd like to be a local and have deep ties to community, possibly Awakened family members if possible. <br /> <br /> What do you all think?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:25:19-07:00","id":1511926,"title":"","content":"What about being part of a Proximi family?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:34:47-07:00","id":1511928,"title":"","content":"Proximi would be easy - I can throw together a Prime-based one to fit Little Atlantis' Hallow-abundance, unless you've got something specific you'd like.<br /> <br /> If you'd prefer an Awakened relative, its the choice between someone who lives here currently or someone who is part of a different Consilium. Your family can be from Little A either way, its just a matter of deciding which Cabal youd have direct ties to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:54:00-07:00","id":1511932,"title":"","content":"Restoring an area that has fallen into disrepair could be a reason they contacted the changelings that will be contracted to renovate the Sanctum. They take a look at the Resonance of the Hallow, plus the lingering effects of the summoning circle, which will probably have a very contrasting ones, and that in itself could lead to exploring more about the Sanctum.<br /> <br /> Exploring the Ruins of the Deep could be another connecting point. Qaf has been told they hold some kind of connection to the angel's warning, but he has been told he is too green to explore them, so the Consilia could probably think its a good idea to have them team up.<br /> <br /> Guiding an Awakening relies on finding a prospect and trying to make them see past the Lie (like the Awakening Gambit do), or being lucky to be at the right place and time. Since it is linked to the forming of the Nimbus, it would probably lead to a major breakthrough for Elpis and a reason why the Mysterium might point them their way.<br /> <br /> So overall, lots of cool ways to cross paths with the cabal.<br /> <br /> In rotes, <i>Control Instincts</i> can be very powerful as a rote, <i>Shaping </i>is an amazing multitool. <i>Command Spirits</i> is a pretty nice safety switch when dealing with spirits, but I think <i>Coaxing the Spirits</i> might be good as well. Having the instant action equivalent of a universal remote control, which can be used event at remote viewing or at a giant scale can be pretty powerful. Activate the safety of all the thug's guns, close all exits to the building, open the vault door, tie a fleeing foe's shoes, turn off the escaping car, it has so many interesting uses.<br /> <br /> Do you have an idea for a Legacy ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-17-2023, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T17:06:23-07:00","id":1511939,"title":"","content":"I was thinking related to Chevalier or one of the Shadowwalkers. Maybe this is a stereotype, but I tend to associate Silver Ladder with silver spoons - high born, emphasis on blood (Malfoys, Black's, Lovegoods, Sabrina's family in Chilling adventures) Maybe a contrast with Ray's working class background. Proximity would be interesting, especially if it tied in with the Ruins mystery. Whatever fits in with setting best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T17:52:25-07:00","id":1511944,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m sure plenty of the Ladder is like that, after all, they are the Pentacle faction most openly interested in power, supernatural or otherwise. And Dynasty and Lineage are a form of power. I like to think of the Ladder having passionate recruits, who truly believe that they will be the ones to tear the Exarchs from the heavens and build a new Great Ladder for the good of all. And as time passes, they start realizing they they almost certainly won\u2019t be the ones to do that, and start focusing on projects that will outlive them, like building dynasties, and finding just the right apprentice to replace them, and so on. Over time, stuff like you described with master-apprentice chains would appear, being politically powerful due to being a descendent, metaphorical or otherwise, of some famous mage. Add Proximi and it\u2019s all a huge mess.<br /> <br /> I think, if the group really believes in Ladder ideology, that they would push the descendants as hard as possible, to better shape them into future leaders of humanity. And pretty much everyone else would have their eyes, and expectations for them as well. Sounds like it\u2019s not a lot of fun. Good background for a character though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T18:21:45-07:00","id":1511946,"title":"","content":"Full disclosure- I lifted the Consilium as a whole from a Prohibition-era game that never got very far. Chevalier's Fallen life was a secretary in the City Hall in that incarnation, and she still has a lot of Flapper trapping when I picture her. Not a problem if you want to use her, just... be aware that I might default to certain things.<br /> <br /> So the local Ladder are mostly nice people, just rather self-absorbed. They think all the world's problems can be solved by Shadow engineering, basically.<br /> <br /> edit: also, is there a Legacy you're going to lean towards? Doesnt have to be set in stone, but I like to start laying the groundwork early","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 05-17-2023, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T19:08:39-07:00","id":1511952,"title":"","content":"My previous post was consumed by the system, but it should be back now.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, one of the best descriptions that I heard for the Th\u00e9archs: The Silver Ladder are priest and humanity is their deity. They want YOU to be exalted, powerful, wise, prosperous and happy. They want humanity to never bend the knee to any gods or monsters. They want to build systems to ensure everyone gets a chance to climb as high up the ladder of creation as they can. They want to throw the gates of the Supernal wide open and make everyone cosmic lords (minus the psychopaths). They are happy to take on the burden of leadership to make it happen, to do the diplomacy, logistics, economics or whatever else is needed to get you there. Some will focus on motivating people to reach higher in life via Cryptopolis, driving them to push against the limits of the Lie. Some might study the Socratic method to become great mentors and councilors. Could that lead down the path of Hubris ? Certainly, but that is the price of ambition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-17-2023, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T21:52:00-07:00","id":1511970,"title":"","content":"Maybe something like this<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1xjHFR7hyhx47ycBlnY3DuYOYqI80NRLW/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1xjHFR7hyhx47ycBlnY3DuYOYqI80NRLW/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1xjHFR7hyhx47ycBlnY3DuYOYqI80NRLW/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1xjHFR7hyhx47ycBlnY3DuYOYqI80NRLW/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I understand about the concillium. Whatever you think works best. I repurpose stuff all the time. Philly is sort of mash of two different characters that I never really got to play in short lived chronicles.<br /> <br /> As I was writing the background it became very Gilmore Girl -esque (if you are familiar with that TV show). I could see a fast talking flapper dame taking Philly under her wing. I think maybe Keepers of the Covenant might be an interesting legacy, but I havn't fully decided yet.<br /> <br /> Are you saying all the world's problems can't be solved by shadow engineering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T23:22:48-07:00","id":1511977,"title":"","content":"Looks fine - Only thing I'd ask you to adjust is the age she Awoke. 14 seems... a bit young. Especially if she's still only Gnosis 1 at this point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T05:25:30-07:00","id":1512001,"title":"","content":"I guess I should have asked this earlier. I read the IC thread, but what are the theme and mood of the chronicle? And what sort of tone are you all aiming for?<br /> It seems like Twin Peaks would be an obvious inspiration for the setting. Anything else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T05:40:10-07:00","id":1512003,"title":"","content":"Never seen Twin Peaks, actually. If I had to guess, parts of it are coming from shows like Eureka and Warehouse 13. And maybe books like House of Blades, The Last Policeman, Recursion, and The Expanse.<br /> <br /> Tone and Theme are a bit hazy right now; I've mostly just been making smaller seeds and letting them grow in response to how Kaiser and Temple react to them. Little Atlantis is a breeding ground for complacency though - no Seers and a shockingly high Hallow-to-Mage ratio. With no-one knowing why, or bothering to look into either matter. So maybe the dangers of complacency and taking things at face value?<br /> <br /> I tend to stay away from the more extreme end of &quot;the whole world sucks&quot; that Chronicles can have --it doesn't need to be worse than our world, just have deeper shadows.<br /> <br /> Temple, Kaiser, you clocking any other themes on your side?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 05-18-2023, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T07:26:07-07:00","id":1512009,"title":"","content":"Never seen Twin Peaks. Hmm. I'd say you should but you've probably been told that lots of times. The Tanis podcast drama is also really good. Also a huge X Files fan, which is not technically set in Pacific NW, but was mostly filmed in Vancoover.<br /> <br /> I'm reading the Expanse right now. Just finished book 4.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you noted the complacency angle. I was worried that I had veered too far in the USA/Hallmark &quot;cozy mystery &quot; direction. Maybe i got it just right. For some reason I also keep thinking of Revenge. I think it's the Bayside town vibe.<br /> <br /> I like mage because it is Late Night Dorm Room Philosophy Majors the RPG. I also like that even though Mages are the most human of the supernatural templates in CoD, they are not not monsters. Hubris is a real thing. Curiosity can kill the cat. And even the most well intentioned mages can do really messed up, terrible things. If you muck around with reality, there will be unintended consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T07:27:45-07:00","id":1512010,"title":"","content":"Its a bit early to know, but if I were to guess one, it would be <i>&quot;Scars of Time&quot;</i>. The scars left behind by Pandora's passing, the lingering echoes cast by the archmage. The fact we met changelings, who have to deal with those of the Durance. The echoes of the Sanctum's previous owners. The setting being a city with a close presence to the Shadow, the realm where those emotional echoes are given form and seek to be promoted. The ruins that contain the secrets of the past that link to something beyond time.It feels like it could go in a very <i>Chrono Cross</i> direction.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Keepers of the Covenant, they are Fate primary and Spirit secondary. So investing in Matter first might delay her progress on the Legacy.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T09:39:50-07:00","id":1512022,"title":"","content":"Well she's 22. Very few twenty-two year olds know what they want to do with their lives. And fate has a way of changing things up on the ones that do.<br /> <br /> I feel like she's starting off on a somewhat solid footing wanting &quot;balence&quot;.<br /> <br /> I did think about taking a dot or two in Destiny, but ran out of merit points. Who knows?<br /> <br /> What more do you want before jumping into the story? Or should Philly just show up at the cottage and start chopping wood for the fireplace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T10:58:02-07:00","id":1512028,"title":"","content":"While just showing up would be funny, I imagine that Elpis is a bit freaked out at the idea what the Shadow reflection of the Cottage is like, and asking around for tips on how to spin it into something positive. They are a bit afraid of the Shadow/Spirits, and so looking for people who might handle it better. I was actually considering having Elpis going to the Shadowwalkers for help later, so this already fits in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T11:29:06-07:00","id":1512030,"title":"","content":"Ok. Well maybe if Philly's mentor is in the Shadowwalkers she might send her. Or maybe there's a bulletin board somewhere for jobs. Or I can imagine a pushy busybody relative giving Elpis her number.<br /> <br /> What do you think? Is Philly working with the Changelings or does she view them as business competition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T12:38:45-07:00","id":1512038,"title":"","content":"If Chevalier (or any of the Shadowwalkers, honestly) is her mentor, then Chevalier could have just prognosticated that joining the Cabal would be a good career move for Philly. In which case, they could be waiting outside Hyleen Cottage &quot;today&quot;, with the Silver Ladder head intending to spin it as a show of goodwill towards the Cabal taking over a plce that is a bit if a black mark towards her order. &quot;Fate Mage says do this&quot; is a bit of a cop-out, but I'm fairly comfortable with the local Order head abusing their Arcana.<br /> <br /> Ethan and Jaye are probably not competition. They're pretty low-key, and mostly invested in fortifying their bar into their own Wyrd safe haven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there'