n Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T16:02:45-07:00","id":1512056,"title":"","content":"Speaking only as a human and not a Mage, I'd probably be checking if the script is an existing language (like a cursive version, since a cursory Google Translate showed nothing) and seeing if any cryptography techniques have any affect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T16:02:58-07:00","id":1512057,"title":"","content":"Also. Do we assume real world landmarks outside Little Atlantis? Like if Philly is hiking, is it Mt. Baker or do we call it something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T16:13:41-07:00","id":1512059,"title":"","content":"I second starting with mundane investigations. Between the cryptographic and occult analysis (both skills we are good with), we may find clues to Linked Mysteries that might help us reduce Opacity.<br /> <br /> Elpis could also use a Ruling of Mind to give us 9-again and I think a Compelling of Time could give us [Potency] extra rolls to our limit, like a version of Patient, allowing us to work at something for a longer period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T16:14:58-07:00","id":1512060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512057#post1512057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also. Do we assume real world landmarks outside Little Atlantis? Like if Philly is hiking, is it Mt. Baker or do we call it something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Geographically I stuck Little Atlantis where a place called <a href=\"https://maps.app.goo.gl/1RTnGfeSa6YeTigF6\" target=\"_blank\">Birch Bay</a> is in the real world. Never been there, but I lived in nearby Bellingham briefly, so my assuption-to-experience ratio was in a nice balance. Assume everything else mirrors the real world pretty closely until something explicitly contradicts it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T17:40:17-07:00","id":1512064,"title":"","content":"I'm going to go ahead and post something in the IC thread and see what you all think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:10:37-07:00","id":1512066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512055#post1512055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another dumb question. Maybe I missed it. How does Elpis identify? I picked up on preferred pronoun being they.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could have sworn I posted it on this thread, but I guess not. Anyways, Agender is probably the best fit. They are kinda perplexed by gender in general. Like they know the concept, and know it\u2019s real for people, but have a hard time applying it to themselves. One of the ways this manifested was picking as their shadow name of a explicitly female goddess, without making the connection that people would make assumptions based on that. They have a tendency to avoid the issue if people make the wrong assumption, gently correcting someone if they think they would be receptive. They tend to keep an anonymous appearance, and wear clothes that conceals their body a lot, in all weathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:15:51-07:00","id":1512067,"title":"","content":"Heads up, the image isn't displaying. Links like the one you used at the end tend to be stable though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T04:25:07-07:00","id":1512109,"title":"","content":"Is that a good place to leave things, with Philly getting a message from Chevalier? Or did you want something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T04:28:59-07:00","id":1512110,"title":"","content":"No, that's good. I'll have a response typed up in the morning (just for context, I live in Japan. At least until August)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T06:41:27-07:00","id":1512113,"title":"","content":"No worries. I'm just stoked. Its been awhile since I got to play Mage. I've been a D&amp;D Paladin for the past year (Which is fine, but D&amp;D is just a different vibe).<br /> Feel free to tell me if I'm doing too much.<br /> I'm US EST. But I'm also a teacher, so I have a lot of free time for the next couple months.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T07:43:54-07:00","id":1512115,"title":"","content":"You all seem like you are more Homebrew Legacy experts than I am. Is there a legacy that recognizes the deep connection between human souls and their enviroments and aim to perfect the fallen world in order to perfect their own souls and encourage awakening for humanity? Something like &quot;Heirs of Eden&quot;- basically trying to recreate paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T08:35:30-07:00","id":1512117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512115#post1512115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You all seem like you are more Homebrew Legacy experts than I am. Is there a legacy that recognizes the deep connection between human souls and their enviroments and aim to perfect the fallen world in order to perfect their own souls and encourage awakening for humanity? Something like &quot;Heirs of Eden&quot;- basically trying to recreate paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443531-2e-legacy-brainstorming?p=1450729#post1450729\">Tamers of Roots</a>. Take a look, see if it\u2019s what you are thinking of. It\u2019s Prime/Life though.<br /> <br /> Edit: As I recall, it\u2019s not a common subject. I remember there being one for being a fisher king style, the land and I are one type thing. I would have to go find it. I think most see the Roses of Eden, or like any of the Spirit legacies and feel it covers the subject enough. The reason I made the Tamers of Root is on the whole I prefer plants to animals, like nodes and Ley lines and felt that flower power wasn\u2019t properly explored in Mage. Maybe you would feel the same toward being connected to the land? If you still can\u2019t find something to your liking, maybe we can make it. Or help you make it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-19-2023, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T09:54:01-07:00","id":1512123,"title":"","content":"Here is a reference to a 2ed conversion of the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page15#post1180101\">Roses of Eden</a>. However, they do not believe in the Atlantean myth, meaning they are usually associated with Nameless Orders, and they have a history of making a mess of Consilium politics, so most mages would be wary. Building on what Temple said, there was a conversion of the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1350259-the-tellurians-an-update\">Tellurians </a>that focuses on becoming a Fisher King, drawing one's kingdoms and subjects closer to the Supernal through benevolent rule. <br /> <br /> I think the main challenge is combining that theme with either a Thyrsus or Silver Ladder Legacy. Perhaps if we can narrow the focus of what this new Eden means and how they approach it, it might be easier to recommend something that resonates with Philly's themes. Right now the only other Legacy that comes to mind is the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors\">Anima Meccanica</a>, which are Silver Ladder and Free Council. They recognize the incredible potential of spirits and push back against the Lie by combining them with technology, incentivizing people to think outside the box. They are solarpunk inventors, which means they have a very natural aesthetic, but I am not sure if you are looking for a technognostic approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T12:24:03-07:00","id":1512132,"title":"","content":"I like the emphasis on plants. I agree that's not something you see as much of in RPGs, probably because its harder to RP i.e. plants don't talk. Which is why I was thinking of incorporating the shadow. In the spirit realm talking to the <a href=\"http://m.youtube.com/watch?v=1n7NB-lPJuU\" target=\"_blank\">spirits of plants, </a>water, stones, etc. is totally something you can do. And its a different feel from the Uratha, and quite frankly many mages who view spirits as &quot;prey&quot;.<br /> <br /> I didn't take any dots in expression because I felt having a larger dice pool for Animal Ken and Persuasion was more mechanically advantageous. But I feel like seeing gardening as an art is something that would be important to Philly. Gardening and landscaping can be very spiritual, especially in many Eastern practices. The same was true in the West before the industrial revolution. <br /> <br /> In the short term, with the Cottage sanctum, I see it playing out like a grown up version of My Neighbor Totoro. Fixing up the house, healing the invisible wounds left by the previous tenants, and befriending/ gaining status with the near by spirit court.<br /> <br /> I feel like both Roses of Eden and Tellurians would take Philly in a darker direction then where she is now. But you never know. It might be interesting for her to meet a Nodding even if she didnt join. In the Seattle game I ST two years ago, the FC were politically ascendant in Seattle, so Atlantis skepticism was typical. Not sure what Cauthon has laid out in this chronicle. I like the idea of &quot;why does the Awakened future have to be a city. Why not a nature reserve?&quot;<br /> <br /> There's time. I'm not really committed to any one idea at this point. I find that stuff comes out in gameplay that you don't expect, and you have to get to know a character for awhile before you find out what they really want.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T13:11:08-07:00","id":1512137,"title":"","content":"So, I chose the skill requirements based on what I was told was the best representations of \u201cGardening\u201d. I was given Survival, Crafts, and Expression. I chose the first two to be a representation of natural knowledge, and working the land to promote growth. Expression was chosen as the main skill, because I thought the creation and cultivation of beauty was a good summation of the legacy\u2026and I wanted to relate singing, and the myth? that plants grow better with sound. What I kinda failed to account for was handling animals, which is kinda important to an ecosystem/garden. (Especially pollinators) So Animal Ken is important to the concept too, and if you wish to replace Expression/Crafts with Animal Ken, I think it works perfectly well. Honestly, if you like the Legacy, and think it fits what you want except for some bits like skills and stuff, you have my permission to modify it however you want.<br /> <br /> I also neglected to think about how the Gardens would impact the Shadow, and how spirits/werewolves might react to Glades becoming more common. That\u2019s a whole side to the legacy that is woefully under-explored. And I now want to take another edit pass on how it affects the Shadow. <br /> <br /> But yeah, we don\u2019t have to decide on anything now. The future isn\u2019t set in stone. Elpis *might* not end up in the Elans, though that\u2019s currently the plan. Personally, I was wondering how shaping themselves towards the Egregore might affect the Legacy process. Elans thrive on hive minds, and the Mysterium kinda constitutes a low level one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-19-2023, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T13:16:42-07:00","id":1512139,"title":"","content":"Oh come up! I even waited for a few minutes before editing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T13:42:22-07:00","id":1512141,"title":"","content":"I think perhaps you are going for a similar feel to <i>Mahou Tsukai no Yome</i> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T13:49:13-07:00","id":1512143,"title":"","content":"Since Chevalier is your Infamous Mentor, do you want to know her Infamy up front, or potentially uncover it over time? I cobbled together a broad-strokes background for her, but if you have something in particular you'd like I can easily adjust fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T17:21:08-07:00","id":1512164,"title":"","content":"Chevalier, a very interesting Shadow Name. It means more than knight in French, its also the first rank of a knight who joined an order. The oaths that sealed the ritual of the Accolade can only be taken by kneeling before a person invested with a symbol of divine authority, such as the holder of the Crown, or the Throne. The Silver Ladder, more than any other Order, make a point of avoiding symbolism of divine rule, so its very interesting they are cool with it. After all, as all mages know, <b>Names Have Power</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T12:00:27-07:00","id":1512232,"title":"","content":"Looks like an interesting manga/anime. I'll have to check it out. Though Philly is not fragile and birdlike. 1.82m, Physical 323, Ath 3.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with Chevalier's infamy being a slow burn, unless its something everyone in the Mage community would know. What rumors would Philly be familiar with?<br /> <br /> Even though I didn't know that I was going to do this until I did, I guess Philly's mother is a thing. I don't have a clear idea in my head as to who are sleepers, sleepwalkers/proximi, and who is awakened in Philly's family. I guess I just liked the idea of having a bunch of quirky, weirdo people getting in her business. Like I said, Gilmore Girls or Arrested Development. What do you think? Does Philly's mom know that she is a mage? And if so, how does she feel about Chevalier? I guess we should hash out how Chevalier became Philly's mentor.<br /> <br /> I also took inheritance, if that makes a difference as to how you want to fit her into the local history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T12:48:36-07:00","id":1512236,"title":"","content":"Rumors... OK, common belief is that she pissed off a temporal Supernal Entity, who knocked her out of Time and erased her timeline. She then reappeared at the climax of a Ticktock Men Y2K End-Of-The-World ritual, where she proceeded to beat the ever-hating shit out of them. While she doesn't confirm or deny any theories, this one seems to be her favorite.<br /> <br /> Alternative theories range from originating in one of the alternate Seattles (though given she's from Chicago, this is harder to explain), to being an Archmage-preserved blackbox of a dead timeline, to being a deep-cover Guardian whose Masque is all kinds of screwed up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T17:56:30-07:00","id":1512242,"title":"","content":"Those are some interesting rumors!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T19:59:40-07:00","id":1512323,"title":"","content":"Temple, Kaiser you all should feel free to RP your research if you want to. I don't want to hog the IC thread.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/