e":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-22T20:10:37-07:00","id":1512403,"title":"","content":"Yep, that's good. I think I'd prefer to keep things out of character for now, so it goes faster. I'm going with Presence and Investigation first, for the Library trip, since Elpis' Wits are low. <br /> <br /> Dragon Bones? Is that in the new book? Haven't had a chance to sit down and read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:08:41-07:00","id":1512436,"title":"","content":"Maybe something with Hesperides for the Cabal Name/Theme, to link up the garden idea with Atlantis/Greek Mythology. And a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladon_(mythology)#:~:text=Ladon%20was%20the%20serpent%2Dlike,and%20carried%20the%20apples%20away.\" target=\"_blank\">dragon</a> guarded the golden apple trees in some versions of the myth!<br /> <br /> Qaf brings in Hebrew/Abrahamic symbolism too though, so Eden/Paradise also works. Although the Hebrew story has a slightly different take on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serpents_in_the_Bible#:~:text=The%20Hebrew%20word%20%D7%A0%D6%B8%D7%97%D6%B8%D7%A9%D7%81%20(N%C4%81%E1%B8%A5%C4%81%C5%A1,particular%20cunning%20in%20its%20deception.\" target=\"_blank\">dragon</a> (It is Chronicles of <b>Darkness</b> after all).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T06:21:15-07:00","id":1512441,"title":"","content":"I didn't intend to go this direction. But stuff comes out when you storytell with other people. Philly is loosely based on two other characters from a previous game, one of whom was a Archaeomantic Acquisitor who's character concept was &quot;Totally NOT Lara Croft&quot;. But the last time that character was heard from she was stuck in the 1960 after being kidnaped by the Angel that assassinated JFK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T09:58:32-07:00","id":1512467,"title":"","content":"Also of interest, if you wanted to add in Celtic symbolism as well<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C3%ADr_na_n%C3%93g\" target=\"_blank\">Tir na nO'g</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T10:07:23-07:00","id":1512468,"title":"","content":"Ooo! In some myths, in order to become King of Tir na NO'g you must defeat the current king in a foot race!<br /> um...hem...world's fastest warrior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T10:30:39-07:00","id":1512470,"title":"","content":"Dragon bones are mentioned in <i> Secrets of the Ruined Temple</i> (which is one of the most helpful references for Atlantean Ruins) and <i>Imperial Mysteries</i>, they are essentially one of the few pieces of evidence that dragons existed.<br /> <br /> Calvin's idea of Ladon sounds pretty cool. I think another option would be to base them on a theme of the <a href=\"https://www.google.com/amp/s/www.atlasobscura.com/articles/sweden-year-walk-arsgang.amp\" target=\"_blank\"> \u00c5rsg\u00e5ng</a>. We would have Qafsiel's theme of overseeing time, Philly's theme of an Ecstatic journey (since its all about going beyond your senses) and Elpis's theme of finding hope by navigating these temporal insights. The myths surrounding it also seem to match the capabilities of the NPCs we know so far. So perhaps our terrific trio intuitively resonate with it and call themselves something like <i>The Year Walkers</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-23-2023, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T11:08:39-07:00","id":1512476,"title":"","content":"Wait Kaiser don\u2019t go, I need your rolls to start the process, since we are teamworking it! I\u2019m the lead, I roll after you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T11:29:39-07:00","id":1512478,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Norse, Scandinavia. Hesperides are often associated with sunsets and the West, but can also be Hyperboria, the far North. Lots to think about. I feel like we can probably RP discussions of cabal symbolism once Philly shows up at the cottage too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T11:39:10-07:00","id":1512481,"title":"","content":"Of course, discussions of dragon bones also makes me think of Iron Fist and the Defenders.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=P0IxqeOP2FU\" target=\"_blank\">Rare paranormal investigator footage</a> of Qafsiel checking some fools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T12:05:17-07:00","id":1512483,"title":"","content":"Our first fight is going to be <i>weird</i>. Qaf can just destroy just about anyone\u2026and Elpis basically can\u2019t fight. Well, I guess they are decent at throwing weapons, but that\u2019s not really a common weapon type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T14:14:10-07:00","id":1512488,"title":"","content":"Philly knows how to use a <a href=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/75iOaMW-pTE/mqdefault.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">chainsaw</a> if that helps","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T14:58:59-07:00","id":1512491,"title":"","content":"Updates might continue to be a little slow on my side, sorry. My mother is visiting, so I'm spending a lot of time driving or taking her sightseeing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T15:17:05-07:00","id":1512492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512491#post1512491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Updates might continue to be a little slow on my side, sorry. My mother is visiting, so I'm spending a lot of time driving or taking her sightseeing</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s cool. I\u2019ve taken, what a week after graduation to truly be ready for Mage? And that was two weeks after finals. And me and Kaiser still need to sort out our rolls. You have fun* with your mom.<br /> <br /> *If hanging out with your mom is, you know, fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T15:18:30-07:00","id":1512493,"title":"","content":"Oh it's fun! My mom speaks Japanese significantly better than I do, so that's a significant stressed off my back<br /> <br /> How's post-graduation going?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T16:41:42-07:00","id":1512503,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s\u2026mixed. I\u2019m relived to be done with school, but job searching isn\u2019t going quickly, and people are scaring me with rent price horror stories. When I calculated the minimum wage I need to make to break even with food, bills, and rent, I got very sad. I\u2019m probably fine, Physics is decently relevant to many jobs, but I worry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T16:49:52-07:00","id":1512504,"title":"","content":"Roommates (or moving in with family) helps significantly. As long as clear parameters and trust is established, at any rate. If possible, look for houses outside cities and commute - DC, for example, is a nightmare to live in but perfectly manageable if you live in Viginia or Maryland at the end of one of the metro lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T18:07:27-07:00","id":1512513,"title":"","content":"Physics is kind of cool. What kind? I'm reading a Fermi biography right now and another book about the Plutonium site in Hanford, WA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T18:19:35-07:00","id":1512516,"title":"","content":"No hurry, enjoy the visit. I wish I could have a chance to practice my Japanese conversation, I studied at a Kumon course years ago and had a blast. Just don't ask me to remember counting conjugations, there are so many edge cases.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the late reply Temple, I posted at the end of my lunch break and can only address this now. I second Cauthon's advice, having roommates cuts down expenses by quite a bit.<br /> <br /> So regarding the rolls, I will make them with a few assumption. Please let me know if I am mistaken and I will reroll them. So they would be:<ul><li>Qaf is using a Compelling of Time (would that be a Ruling instead ? I think Compelling could be used to intensify the time a person can stay on task) to give both of us one extra roll on extended actions by granting the Patient merit. Duration primary, advanced duration, High Speech for a second person.</li> <li>Elpis is using a Ruling of Mind to grant 9-again in our rolls.</li> <li>A single Willpower is available per roll. Not sure about this one, since the interval since chapter one and time per roll is wibbly-wobbly at the moment.</li> </ul><br /> So Qaf has an Int of 2, Occult of 4 and Investigation of 4. Which means a maximum of 7 (Int + Skill + Time spell) rolls at a dice pool of 9 (Int + Skill + Willpower):<br /> <br /> <i>Investigation</i>:<ul><li><i>First</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>10</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 6, 6, 3, 3, 1, 7, 6 -&gt; 4 successes</li> <li><i>Second</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>10</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 6, 6, 3, 3, <b>10</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>9</b>, 5, <b>10</b>, 7 -&gt; 9 successes <b>(E)</b></li> <li><i>Third</i>: 6, 5, 5, 5, 4, 3, 3, 2, 1 -&gt; Fail</li> <li><i>Fourth</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>8</b>, 7, 7, 6, 6, 4, 1, 3, 1 -&gt; 3 successes</li> <li><i>Fifth</i>: <b>9</b>, <b>8</b>, 6, 4, 3, 3, 2, 1, 1, 1-&gt; 2 successes</li> <li><i>Sixth</i>: <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 2, 1-&gt; 2 successes</li> <li><i>Seventh</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 7, 7, 6, 6, 5, 1, 3-&gt; 3 successes</li> </ul><br /> <i>Occult</i>:<ul><li><i>First</i>: 7, 6, 5, 5, 5, 3, 2, 2, 2 -&gt; Fail</li> <li><i>Second</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 7, 5, 5, <b>10</b>, 6, 3, <b>10</b>, 5-&gt; 8 successes <b>(E)</b></li> <li><i>Third</i>: 7, 7, 7, 5, 3, 3, 3, 2, 1 -&gt; Fail</li> <li><i>Fourth</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 7, 6, 5, 5, 2, <b>9</b>, 3, 5-&gt; 5 successes <b>(E)</b></li> <li><i>Fifth</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>8</b>, <b>8</b>, 6, 6, 5, 3, 3, 1, <b>8</b>-&gt; 4 successes</li> <li><i>Sixth</i>: <b>10</b>, <b>9</b>, <b>8</b>, 6, 4, 4, 4, 4, 3, <b>8</b>, 3-&gt; 3 successes</li> <li><i>Seventh</i>: 6, 6, 6, 5, 5, 4, 4, 3, 3 -&gt; Fail</li> </ul>Those rolls are all over the place. I don't remember the rules for secondary actors in extended actions, so I just checked the rules on CofD page 72. Seems like fails just don't add to Elpis successes. I think we only get a Condition if Elpis fails a roll, no clue what an exceptional success does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-23-2023, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T18:46:21-07:00","id":1512520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512481#post1512481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, discussions of dragon bones also makes me think of Iron Fist and the Defenders.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=P0IxqeOP2FU\" target=\"_blank\">Rare paranormal investigator footage</a> of Qafsiel checking some fools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, seems about right. This would be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ogHdcW57JvM\" target=\"_blank\">Qaf in chase combat</a>.<br /> <br /> I think Philly doesn't have <i>Machine Invisibility</i> or a way to carry the chainsaw unnoticed, so she will need a strategy for that. But if she does have one, it has 9 again, meaning all she needs is one good hit to annihilate the morale of the opposing team. She also has good stealth, which means she can make some of the most terrifying opening moves.<br /> <br /> Elpis has pretty good stealth, so they have a way to avoid combat or start it on their own terms (which means the cabal has a predisposition for sneaking around), with <i>Invisibility</i> and <i>Control Sound</i> covering everything else. I think they will also need to rely on the pepper spray, which can apply a major penalty if it hits. Magic wise, Shielding is strong, one of Forces can render many mundane sources of damage harmless. A Potency 2 one could protect from kinetic and heat damage, meaning punches, guns, flamethrowers and so on would be toothless if they don't care about The Curse. Apart from that, I think taking items that they could synergize with Compelling spells would provide a lot of options. I remember reading <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2019/06/1-mage-awakening-2e-13-practices-of.html\" target=\"_blank\">this article</a> a while ago and it had some fascinating ideas on how to use the Practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-23-2023, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T19:00:35-07:00","id":1512526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512513#post1512513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physics is kind of cool. What kind? I'm reading a Fermi biography right now and another book about the Plutonium site in Hanford, WA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it\u2019s just a Bachelors, it\u2019s a generic physics degree, which meant I studied a bit of everything. If I had my way though, I would have spent all my time on Astrophysics and Gravity. I love stars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T20:01:58-07:00","id":1512531,"title":"","content":"Kaiser...what is with those rolls? The Heck?... Sometimes I forget just how focused Qaf is on specific skills.<br /> <br /> Yeah, ok good assumptions. I think Ruling is fine for both Creative Thaumaturgy. As for willpower costs...we will wing it for now.<br /> <br /> Anyways, so for the Library Investigation, Investigation 2 + Presence 3 = 5....which seems...low. Oh...whoops. Research Is Intelligence + Academics according to Mage 2e pg 208. If that's the case, uh the base pool is Intelligence 4 + Academics 3 +1 Research specialty = 8, 11 with willpower. Oh whatever, I'm going to use the dice pool Cauthon listed. With Kaiser's rolls, and Elpis' will, we will do fine.<br /> <br /> Elpis already has the Patient merit...don't know if that stacks but whatever<br /> <br /> Investigation: base = 3 pre + Inv 2 + 3 Will = 8 dice<ul><li>First: +4 dice-&gt; 12 pool-&gt; [5 5 4 6 5 5 5 1 1 2 10 8] [9 10 8]-&gt; 5 successes (E) + 0 ([1 3]) = 5</li> <li>Second: +9?-&gt; 17?-&gt;[6 9 3 7 9 3 7 4 9 1 3 7 2 5 2 4 1] [7 9 7 9 3] -&gt; 5 successes (E) + 1 ([8 2]) = 6</li> <li>Third: +0-&gt;8 -&gt; [7 4 10 2 2 3 9 5][2 8]-&gt; 3 Successes</li> <li>Fourth: +3-&gt;11-&gt; [7 3 7 9 1 6 8 7 3 5 9] [1 1] -&gt; 3 successes</li> <li>Fifth: +2-&gt; 10-&gt; [10 3 9 3 5 1 9 2 6 8][5 7 9 9 6]-&gt; 6 successes (E) + 0 ([7 2]) = 5</li> <li>Sixth: +2-&gt; 10-&gt;[4 6 10 8 2 7 8 8 3 2] [1]-&gt; 4 successes</li> </ul>Occult: base = 4 int + 3 Occ + 3 Will = 10<ul><li>First: +0-&gt;10-&gt; [7 4 5 2 10 10 4 6 6 4][8 4] -&gt; 3 successes</li> <li>Second: +8-&gt; 18-&gt; [1 8 6 5 4 10 4 2 1 5 3 6 9 6 6 1 2 6] [2 4] -&gt; 3 successes</li> <li>Third: +0-&gt;10-&gt; [1 9 2 8 3 5 9 2 5 4][5 8]-&gt; 4 successes</li> <li>Fourth: +5-&gt;15-&gt;[3 9 1 9 5 9 4 10 3 4 8 2 2 4 2][9 9 5 9 8 5 2]-&gt; 9 successes (E) + 0 ([1 6 3]) = 9</li> <li>Fifth: +4-&gt;14-&gt;[10 2 10 7 2 5 6 1 7 9 2 10 5 3][3 6 10 9 1 9 2]-&gt; 7 successes (E) + 0 ([4 2 7]) = 7</li> <li>Sixth: +3-&gt;13-&gt; [3 7 7 1 4 10 3 7 5 6 1 6 6][3]-&gt;1 successes</li> <li>Seventh: +0-&gt;10-&gt;[5 1 8 5 9 10 3 5 1 9] [8 9 10 9 5 8] -&gt; 9 successes (E) + 2 ([5 10 2][8]) = 11</li> </ul>And you know what I just realized? The program I'm using to roll doesn't account for 10/9/8 again on the second set. doing it manually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T20:18:29-07:00","id":1512534,"title":"","content":"I recommend the Onyx Dice app, its pretty intuitive and accounts for the rules. I think you forgot one Investigation roll.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Qaf is a generalist on Arcana knowledge and a specialist in mundane one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</spa