hankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T20:48:50-07:00","id":1512537,"title":"","content":"I forgot Patient added 2 as well, that is some great cost benefit. I am a bit confused about Elpis' max tries:<br /> <br /> Investigation: 4 (Int) + 3 (Academics) + 2 (Patient) = 9 rolls<br /> <br /> Occult: 4 (Int) + 3 (Occult) + 2 (Patient) = 9 rolls<br /> <br /> I think you may have 2 more rolls available for each. With the exceptional successes so far, I think Elpis could take the extra successes option and tear through the research in record time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T21:21:28-07:00","id":1512541,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m using the stats provided by Cauthon when asking what to roll for this aka Presence + Investigation. Which added up to 5. Making my max rolls 7 on the investigation bit. You are correct, Intelligence + Academics is much better for Elpis, especially because of their specialty in research making it 10 rolls. However I\u2019d rather go with what Cauthon said about the rolls previously until updated on it. I mean, I\u2019m reasonably sure it only took one or two tries, and going past 7 is waaaaay overkill, but I will update it with the rest if you wish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T06:32:38-07:00","id":1512566,"title":"","content":"Gosh. Formal Dining. Can Philly use shaping with a reach 1 to change clothes, or would a matter veiling spell be better? Or does she not have time to do that before going through the portal? Otherwise she is still in hiking clothes and hasn't showered recently. Might want to cast Body Control to eliminate BO and Mutable Mask to fix hair. If she doesn't change before going through portal, maybe she would use the restroom?<br /> <br /> Do you want me to roll anything to see if I am recognized by Maurice or other staff and patrons? I also have Striking Looks **, Fame * (Small Town), and Order Status *. Might want to roll Presence + Composure for Good Impression, and Wits + Socialize for fitting in.<br /> <br /> Intelligence + Occult I guess for recalling details about Hyleen Cottage and the Corenne?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T06:57:29-07:00","id":1512569,"title":"","content":"I was sort of kidding about the chainsaw. Pretty sure Cauthon would make me roll weapons rather than crafts for that. And weapons is untrained for Philly (although for certain character builds chainsaw fighting would be an awesome skill specialty/ fighting style merit).There are lots of other ways to mess someone up with Life 2, Spirit 2, and Matter 2, especially if you don't care about hubris or paradox. Philly also has brawl 1 and firearms 1, and archery technically falls under Athletics, which for her is 3 (and she did spend a lot of time at Ladder summer camp).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T06:59:56-07:00","id":1512570,"title":"","content":"Y'all are so detailed with your rolls. I love it. If you havn't noticed, I'm a story/character/worldbuilding kind of dude. I'll have to up my rules crunch game to keep up with you all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T09:04:39-07:00","id":1512585,"title":"","content":"Since there were a lot of rolls, I wanted to make sure the info could be easily referenced. That being said, roleplay is just as important to me.<br /> <br /> I think <i>Shaping</i> might need a Crafts roll and the Reach option to quickly turn it into another outfit. But a Veiling should solve the issue nicely for its duration.<br /> <br /> I believe a Potency primary Ruling of Matter and Life could cover all the cleaning a mage could ever need (operating on similar mechanics as <i>Purge Illness</i>), both for personal grooming or sanitizing an area.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:20:18-07:00","id":1512614,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">So maybe something like this? Assuming the spells are feasible in RP time allotted. I don't want to invoke paradox from sleeper quiescence. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Bibbidi-Bobbidi-Boo</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Intent: to create the illusion of one form of attire and grooming instead of another i.e. clothes, accessories, shoes, hair and makeup</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Veiling: Matter (1 manna required) + Life</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Improvised</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Duration: Advanced (1 scene)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Casting Time: Advanced (instant)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">({[Gnosis (1) + Arcanum/Practice (2) \u2013 2<sup>nd</sup> Arcanum (-2)] + 2 High Speech} + Willpower (+3))</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2 reaches (Advanced Duration + Instant Casting Time) = 1 free + 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spend two manna, one for common Arcanum and one to mitigate paradox penalty of 2</span><sup>nd</sup><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> reach</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">[3,3,5,7,10,10,7,10] 3 Successes</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Body Control (Life \u2022\u2022)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Intent: to eliminate body odor and bad breath</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Practice: Ruling</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Primary Factor: Duration (1 scene)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Improvised</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Casting Time: Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">1 (Gnosis) +2 (Life) + 2 (High Speech) = 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Spend manna for 2<sup>nd</sup> reach</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">[4,5,8,8,10,6] 3 Successes</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Good Impression</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">3 (Presence) +3 (Composure)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">[1,5,6,6,7,8] 1 success</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Fit in</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2 (Wits) +2 (Socialize) +1 (Striking Looks) +1 (Fame)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">[1,2,3,3,5,5] Take beat for dramatic failure</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Recall Occult History</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">2+2+1 (Order Status)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">[2,3,4,8,8]</span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T12:36:34-07:00","id":1512619,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't mean to imply that it wasn't. Both of you are great at describing imagos and mage sight. It makes the magic seem more real and immersive. I was just saying you are on point. Not slackers like I normally am.<br /> <br /> Funny story. I also used to live in DC. And one evening I had just gotten off work, and I'm like in cargo shorts, work boots, and a t shirt, covered in sweat. And my buddy calls me up and says &quot;Hey its my birthday, and my mom sent me a blank check to go out to dinner. Want to come&quot; So I'm like sure, but... and he's like don't worry about it. So we show up at this restaurant in Georgetown (Where rich people eat dinner). My buddy's also in shorts and a t-shirt with flip-flops. And we walk in. And I swear, everyone including the maitre'd and all the wait staff are in like tuxedos or formal wear. I'm surprised they didn't just tell us to get lost. But he seated us anyhow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T14:04:45-07:00","id":1512628,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure if it's a dual arcana spell where only one is ruling, it doesn't have a mana cost. I don't think it's a combined spell? Just a duel requirement one, so no penalty is needed for the first spell. (Also, we can't do combined spells yet, since we all are Gnosis 1, and I think it's gnosis 3 before we can. Multi arcana spells are fine though.)<br /> <br /> Everything else checks out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T14:05:55-07:00","id":1512629,"title":"","content":"What do you all think would be a good Thrysus proximity family curse. I'm struggling to think of one? Maybe something to do with Spirits, or maybe a hereditary disease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T14:15:37-07:00","id":1512632,"title":"","content":"I agree, I think you don't need to pay the mana cost. A combined spell is about having two unrelated effects using the same combined Imago, which requires a minimum of Gnosis 3 (core book page 86). This one is a custom spell using two Arcana, so no need for the penalty. But otherwise it looks good to go.<br /> <br /> <i>Body Control </i>seems to be over Reaching by two, since its a Ruling, which means only one free Reach at Life 2. Philly would need one Reach to go over her spell control (since she cast the <i>Bibbidi-Bobbidy-Boo</i> first), one for instant use and one for advanced duration. However, I think a Potency primary Life and Matter spell could be used to remove all dirt, sweat, bacteria and similar, which can be used both to clean and sanitize (diminishing the severity of pathogens in the area by Potency). Using that will allow her to instantly clean up without having to sustain an effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T17:17:50-07:00","id":1512656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512541#post1512541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m using the stats provided by Cauthon when asking what to roll for this aka Presence + Investigation. Which added up to 5. Making my max rolls 7 on the investigation bit. You are correct, Intelligence + Academics is much better for Elpis, especially because of their specialty in research making it 10 rolls. However I\u2019d rather go with what Cauthon said about the rolls previously until updated on it. I mean, I\u2019m reasonably sure it only took one or two tries, and going past 7 is waaaaay overkill, but I will update it with the rest if you wish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shoot, Academics. Eeeeh, realistically Academics won't help with this specifically. The Book does jot respond well to academia.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512566#post1512566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gosh. Formal Dining. Can Philly use shaping with a reach 1 to change clothes, or would a matter veiling spell be better? Or does she not have time to do that before going through the portal? Otherwise she is still in hiking clothes and hasn't showered recently. Might want to cast Body Control to eliminate BO and Mutable Mask to fix hair. If she doesn't change before going through portal, maybe she would use the restroom?<br /> <br /> Do you want me to roll anything to see if I am recognized by Maurice or other staff and patrons? I also have Striking Looks **, Fame * (Small Town), and Order Status *. Might want to roll Presence + Composure for Good Impression, and Wits + Socialize for fitting in.<br /> <br /> Intelligence + Occult I guess for recalling details about Hyleen Cottage and the Corenne?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/877640-creative-thaumaturgy-fallen-world-edition?p=1472640#post1472640\">Here's a general cleaning spell</a>. Only real downside is that the detritus sloughs off you rather than vanishes.<br /> <br /> Most people in the Rose right now are not affiliated in any way with the Consilium, and Chevalier's table is out of the way. Since they're talking Order buisness, it's mostly secure from scrutiny (This won't always be the case, just simplifying things for your intro)<br /> <br /> Rolling is fine, or you can opt to not know much. General anyone-in-the-order-knows-this is that the Corenne were Left-Handed, their name means &quot;The Return(ing)&quot; in High Speech, and that their bloody purging is what moved the Consilium to being more Guardian run. By mutual agreement, that last one, as opposed to Guardians pressuring for control. The Cottage was put in common trust because no-one wanted to deal with the legacy of it at the time, and theres plenty of stronger Hallows for claiming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512619#post1512619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny story. I also used to live in DC. And one evening I had just gotten off work, and I'm like in cargo shorts, work boots, and a t shirt, covered in sweat. And my buddy calls me up and says &quot;Hey its my birthday, and my mom sent me a blank check to go out to dinner. Want to come&quot; So I'm like sure, but... and he's like don't worry about it. So we show up at this restaurant in Georgetown (Where rich people eat dinner). My buddy's also in shorts and a t-shirt with flip-flops. And we walk in. And I swear, everyone including the maitre'd and all the wait staff are in like tuxedos or formal wear. I'm surprised they didn't just tell us to get lost. But he seated us anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Georgetown is used to rowdy college kids coming through. I say this as someone who went to college in DC (American University, but our ROTC program was a satellite to Georgetown's so we had a lot of interaction with them)<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512628#post1512628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure if it's a dual arcana spell where only one is ruling, it doesn't have a mana cost. I don't think it's a combined spell? Just a duel requirement one, so no penalty is needed for the first spell. (Also, we can't do combined spells yet, since we all are Gnosis 1, and I think it's gnosis 3 before we can. Multi arcana spells are fine though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it still costs the requisite Mana if you incorporate a non-Ruling. Makes Praxis and Rotes much more valuable. I'm open to negotiating that point though, I don't think the rules were explicit on the delineation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T17:55:21-07:00","id":1512661,"title":"","content":"No, looks like they were not specific on mana costs on multi-arcana spells at all. Which leads me to wonder where I got the idea from. Oh well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T10:00:26-07:00","id":1512745,"title":"","content":"I imagine every th\u00e9arch had to face a variation of this situation at some point, which is probably why Dr Who style psychic paper would be a highly requested item of Order crafters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T10:57:08-07:00","id":1512749,"title":"","content":"Another Dumb Question: Did you all share character sheets and I just missed it somewhere, or are we keeping those secret?<br /> <br /> Still thinking through Philly's background and Proximi family stuff. I sent some things to Cauthon to make sure nothing was chronicle breaking, but I want to get you all's imput too.<br /> <br /> Philly is the only awakened member of her immediate family, but she has a few mage relatives. She is the descendent of two proximi bloodlines (I'm going very Bene Gesserit here).<br /> Her mother's proximi dynasty is Thyrsus path. They emigrated from Greece after World War II and eventually ended up going west. Some Ladder mages claim, without much evidence, that the bloodline goes all the way back to the fall of Atlantis. The sleepers and sleepwalkers in the family tend to be very open to non-western spiritual traditions, esoterica, and magic. Basically Hippies with money. Probably ties to the agriculture community. Not sure what their curse should be.<br /> <br /> Her dad's family is a Moros path dynasty that moved west with the Transcontinental railroad (DE 2 inspired here). They are mostly interested in making money, and whatever their curse is they rarely discuss it. Something to do with iron and machines.<br /> <br /> I've also been thinking about cabal dynamics. Elpis is from Seattle. How long have they lived in Little Atlantis? And Qaf grew up there. Would he know Philly already? It's a small town, but they are also sort of from opposite sides of the tracks so to speak.<br /> <br /> I'm not fully committed to any of this by the way, if you all have a really cool idea. Mechanics wise I'm working with Order status 1, Fame 1 (Small Town), Resources 3, Infamous Mentor 1, Inheritance 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T14:30:01-07:00","id":1512772,"title":"","content":"We originally started brainstorming the chronicle's ideas and character concepts over private messages. I use <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/cofd.html#awakening\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's dynamic character sheets</a>, but both Temple and I were having trouble uploading them to the chat. If I remember correctly, I think Cauthon has a link for a folder with all of them.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what the Curse could be. Proximi are very cool, but its difficult to find a nice balance between notable and crippling when designing the aspects of the Curse, so even homebrews are rare. Thyrsus wise, the Sisters of the Mountain are one, but are linked to the Appalachian mountains, the Essers from <i>Night Horrors: Conquering Heroes</i> are the only other ones I know. Regarding homebrew ideas, her mother's Dynasty could be from Rhodes, Greece. She could have Forces as her third Arcanum, with a Curse involving sunlight or spirits linked to Helios. Make them descendants of the mythological sea nymph that became Rhodes island.<br /> <br /> Looking at the document you shared, I think Philly has a pretty high chance of having met Qaf's mundane persona. Here are some opportunities that come to mind:<ul><li>Qaf works at the Raven &amp; Rose as a bouncer during the high season.</li> <li>She could have seen him in a sports competition (marathon, triathlon, etc), since Philly has the skill of a professional athlete.</li> <li>He is a self defense teacher in Little Atlantis, so she may have attended a class.</li> <li>He runs with his dog every morning, so they may have met when he was jogging, biking or hiking.</li> <li>He enjoys swimming and scuba diving, they may have met at the beach.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-25-2023, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:35:34-07:00","id":1512801,"title":"","content":"I think the Rhodes idea is kind of cool. My main experience with legacies is as a ST, not as a player. I ST a chronicle in Seattle where one of the PC was a metropolitan (which lead to interesting results, as one may imagine). I think a Spirit based curse is the way to go. I've been thinking a lot about how Philly perceives the the Shadow, similar to Qaf and clocks, or Elpis and the night sky/stars. That's kind of why I wanted to get a better handle on the Proximi thing, because I think it would have a big influence on her use of symbolism. One of my goals, half way between character concept and out-of-character aspiration is to explore more how family influences a mages use of magic and interaction with mage society. My old game group I think tended to treat order as more of an abstract concept rather than a lived social experience. <br /> <br /> I think all of those, or at least one of those, is a very plausible way for Philly and Qaf's mundane personas to know each other, so I will try to incorporate that into her conversation with Chevalier and their first meeting. Especially since Qaf is three or four years older than Philly it is very possible that he knew her before she awakened, so it might be interesting to role play that out. I kind of envisioned Philly's awakening being sort of a radical change in her persona. Did Qaf attend LAU? I changed things around from what I had before. Philly awakened before the beginning of college, not high school. If Elpis also attended LAU that would be a connection between them and Philly also.<br /> <br /> I guess 3 dots is technically &quot;professional athlete&quot; level. I guess I was envisioning like competitive college sports. If she was doing cross country or 800 M, there would definitely be a connection to Qaf, as well as swimming. I have three friends who do sea swimming IRL. There's only one MA studio in town probably so definitely a connection there, though she only has one dot in brawl, so vastly different belt/skill levels. Honestly I was thinking it was probably like a beginners level self defense class. But maybe if she and Qaf are in the same cabal, she will develop that skill more. I was thinking freediving rather than scuba, which is a heck of a lot easier with life magic. Gotta get that manna at the bottom of the quarry somehow.<br /> <br /> Philly is definitely going to be excited that Qaf has a dog!<br /> <br /> I guess I was just confirming that we had a nice balance of intellectual, physical, and social attributes and skills. I think Philly will probably see Elpis as kind of intimidating since she sees herself as being primarily a preppy jock. Elpis has actually been studying something for the past four years instead of making gentleman C's and going to parties. I don't' think Philly went to the library once while she was there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T18:15:22-07:00","id":1512805,"title":"","content":"I think Qaf would have studied in LAU for something like a self defense certification or fitness instruction, since he dreams of having his own martial arts school, but he is still is building capital and developing his own style. The <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> core book has a baseline for skills, along with detailed rules and equipment information, plus lots of interesting GM plots, its a very easy recommendation. But anyway, when looking at skills the baseline is:<br /> <br /> \u25cf - <b>Basic Competency:</b> You took a shooting class (Firearms), take better care of yourself than most people (Athletics), understand a few forensic techniques (Investigation)<br /> \u25cf\u25cf - <b>Professional Skill:</b> You could earn a living with your degree of knowledge, you have a solid, reliable level of ability.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>National Level Expert:</b> You are considered an expert at what you do and a reference in your skill.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>Global Tier Master:</b> You have enough mastery to be a mover and shaker in your field, being considered on par with the world's leading experts.<br /> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - <b>Peak Human Ability:</b> You can deduce like Sherlock Holmes (Investigation), cook on par with Gordon Ramsay (Crafts) or snipe like Simo Hahya (firearms).<br /> <br /> However, keep in mind that style merits can still account for a massive gap in efficiency, such as having a fighting style making you spend far less Willpower, professional training giving more consistent results or even having done all the work to have an air tight Alternative Identity when spying. There are also highly skilled experts in the shadows, so who knows who you may run into.<br /> <br /> When thinking about the Shadow, there is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/179059-what-does-the-shadow-look-like?p=180787#post180787\">one description that I found very evocative</a>, maybe it can prove helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-25-2023, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T06:38:32-07:00","id":1512862,"title":"","content":"I've also been thinking about the cottage. Elpis and Qaf have already started exploring the mystery of the cottage (&quot;every hallow has a story&quot;), and Philly will have to catch up when she gets there. One of her character asperations, very much in keeping with Silver Ladder, is to improve a sanctum in both its mundane and supernatural aspects. To wit:<br /> 1. Repairing, furnishing, remodeling the cottage, adding a garden and animal friendly features (Crafts and Resources)<br /> 2. Increasing its mundane and supernatural security<br /> 3. Creating environmental yantras that aide the cabal<br /> 4. Maybe creating a cabal library?<br /> 5. Cool Artifacts?<br /> <br /> More long term goals might be acquiring Pandora's soul stone, or some other soul stone, and creating a demesne, linking the cottage to a node, somehow increasing its hallow potency, and establishing some sort of agreement or status with the spirit court in the immediate area, creating a verge to the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts or suggestions on these. What were you all thinking?<br /> <br /> Obviously some of this is contingent on how the mystery of the cottage's connection to the Corenne and the Ruins in the Deep plays out, and how long Elpis, Qaf, and Philly end up staying there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T09:56:33-07:00","id":1512886,"title":"","content":"I think those sound pretty cool, I had some rough outlines of ideas that may compliment them:<ul><li>Regarding looks, I was thinking of leveraging the stonework to focus on a rustic, comfortable and well lit design, more cut stone than cobblestone. But I have no idea if that is a look the cabal would go for.</li> <li>Dog friendly would be cool.</li> <li>Regarding rooms, we have no full idea on dimensions and we have to account on the attention avoidance spell. But some broad strokes ideas would be:<ul><li>Summoning and imbuing room, made from the heavily warded one on the second floor.</li> <li>Material storage for magic components and summoning room paraphernalia (summoning the cherubim of lost minds needs different components than the summoning of the totem of strategy).</li> <li>A small studio to store books, Grimmoires, maps and generally do research.</li> <li>Heavily warded area for Artifact study/storage and experiments. It would allow us to test and record our research and new spells for later use.</li> <li>Training facilities, who knows what we will go up against or if we will need to be ready for a Duel Arcane.</li> <li>Supplies, like preserved food for emergencies, first aid kit (anti burn cream in the kitchen) and a fire extinguisher.</li> <li>Security, as you mentioned, mundane would be great, but if Philly could negotiate to haver some guardian spirits as well, it would be even better.</li> </ul></li> <li>Obtaining Pandora's soul stone would be a major win for Elpis, but also quite the political feat. We need to convince the Guardians that we both need it and can adequately keep it contained, especially since Rapt souls stones are dangerous. But it may lead to a major breakthrough on what happened to Pandora and, since she was an Elan, may also allow us to have access to a Mind Anullitiy.</li> <li>We should probably setup a discrete, yet well defended cloud server on our research materials, in case they are stolen. I think the Orders in general would have good practices for that, but I imagine Elpis might have learned as part of their mystagogue training.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T10:46:55-07:00","id":1512892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1amFrn14M7LXlLitxNxEpc0rm1e8jCtD5/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1amFrn14M7LXlLitxNxEpc0rm1e8jCtD5/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1amFrn14M7LXlLitxNxEpc0rm1e8jCtD5/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1amFrn14M7LXlLitxNxEpc0rm1e8jCtD5/edit?usp=sharing&amp;ouid=117362549266880055196&amp;rtpof=true&amp;sd=true </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> I made a doc of everything already described about the house. Feel free to edit if I missed something.<br /> <br /> The initial description mentioned a basement, but Elpis and Qaf did not explore that part of the house IC, and we dont' know how it is accessed (external cellar door?). No mention of a bathroom. If the house was built in the 1930s and hasn't been used since the 50s, it might not have one (Outhouse?). But I took the liberty of a suggested location for one in the draft floor plan. I also took the liberty of supposing that maybe the house has a wood burning stove. (Dimensions are based on the assumption that front door in picture is a modern standard sized door)<br /> <br /> It should be noted that in the picture the house exterior is wooden shingles. Maybe Kaiser was thinking the foundation is stone? That would make sense. Also the gable of the attic floor slopes inward, so the front bedroom and the summoning room would have slanted ceilings (important especially for Qaf and Philly to note). <br /> <br /> There are neighboring houses visibly near by, but there wasn't a description of the yard. I suppose if the cabal really decides to make a go of it and stay for awhile, extensive renovations to enlarge the house and add rooms are possible (mundanely, or with the help of a Mastigos friend). At the very least probably add a shed and maybe a detached garage. Also wondering about zoning. Like could Philly have chickens, a goat, etc? Also I was thinking Philly would want a good tree (Apple?), maybe with a guardian spirit attached - that could be a mystery/chapter in of itself.<br /> <br /> I like all the strategic defense thinking. Very Arrow. Of course a lot of this could be RP IC. I just wanted to get the ball rolling/couldn't stop thinking about it.<br /> <br /> Temple, what were your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:00:15-07:00","id":1512896,"title":"","content":"If Philly planted an Apple tree she would need life patterning to accelerate its growth.<br /> <br /> I was reading Terrence Mckenna a few months ago, so I have all kinds of weird plant ideas right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T13:52:22-07:00","id":1512907,"title":"","content":"Having an apple tree could be used by Philly to make a statement, because the name Avalon means island of apples. It is associated with the Walker in Mists called Emrys, The Merlin of Arthurian legend and a confirmed archmage of the Silver Ladder.<br /> <br /> Oak is another candidate, it is associated with medicine, strength and protection. Rowan guards against malicious spells. The olive tree might be another option, since its symbolically tied with wisdom, endurance (it can grow in the most barren soil), versatility (since every part can be used), peace (giving an olive branch) and long term support of civilization (the foundation myth of Athens).\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T15:44:33-07:00","id":1512920,"title":"","content":"Oh shoot-I was summoned! Sorry!<br /> <br /> Uh. Well Kaiser and Calvin mostly covered my initial thoughts on the house. Rapt soul stones are dangerous, needs warding, dogs need places they are comfortable, etc. As for my own thoughts.<ul><li>I don\u2019t remember if we already checked, but it\u2019s possible the Hallow is not at its peak. We should check in on that at a later date.</li> <li>We could also try and make a node, I bet Philly would appreciate the effects of a Life Node\u2026maybe as part of finding a Guardian Spirit.</li> <li>I\u2019d like to set up a spell that blocks light pollution, and stuff. It makes a nice yantra, and is pretty.</li> <li>We might need a\u2026stasis point for extended astral journeys. Nothing quite like ruining one\u2019s health because your body technically just sat in one place for a few days.</li> </ul>I need to bush up on my tree symbolism before I really weigh in, but I\u2019m partial to the olive as of the moment. I also really need to look up common trees in that part of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T16:03:02-07:00","id":1512922,"title":"","content":"After we learn more about the Hallow's history and have a better idea of what forces we are poking, how about using Occult rolls to apply feng shui to try to facilitate the ley energy's flow or modify its Resonance ? Its slower than the dedicated Prime spells, but it might be an interesting experiment to test. Since we have two Prime mages and one Spirit mage, we can keep detailed track of progress very easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T08:38:36-07:00","id":1512963,"title":"","content":"Absolutely agree about the light pollution thing. IRL it makes me sad when I can't see stars at night, and IC I think Philly felt the same thing returning to Little A from her journey in the mountains. Not sure exactly how far out from Old Town the Heights is, but even a little bit of light pollution can often spoil a night sky. Would the cabal need space magic for that, or maybe forces could enhance the illumination of stars?<br /> <br /> Depending on the size of the property, I don't see why the cabal couldn't plant all the different kinds of trees Kaiser mentions. Also remember that according to Cauthon's description many of the other houses in the neighborhood are abandoned and falling down, so sleepers might not notice if the cabal made changes to other properties around Hyleen Cottage.<br /> <br /> Centering a whole arc of a chronicle on a cabal's sanctuary might be unusual, but I think it could be fun. Lots of mysteries to explore, and wisdom choices to make: whether to try and get Pandora's soul stone back and use it; whether to get rid of the summoning circle in the attic, and so on. Also there is a political aspect to it. If we start altering ley lines or making significant changes to the Shadow landscape we might come into conflict with the other cabals or even the Uratha pack. Do we know whether they are primarily Bone Shadows or Hunters in Darkness?<br /> <br /> The Astral angle is interesting. Mind is Phily's inferior Arcanum, so she might have misgivings about accessing her Astral Path. I feel like what I know about her already, she probably has some scary Goetia, and I think Proximi probably have really weird interactions with the Astral (think about Alia in the Dune books). BtP is the CoD that I know the least about, so maybe something with the Primordial Dream would be interesting, and it might give Philly insight into her path. And of course it is interesting to explore the similarities and differences between the Anima Mundi and the Shadow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T08:52:32-07:00","id":1512964,"title":"","content":"And then of course there are lots of other mysteries too. I was thinking about the Factory the other day. What's going on there? Seers, Hunters, GM Infrastructure? Or something even weirder, like a Promethean or Deviant Laboratory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T09:02:21-07:00","id":1512965,"title":"","content":"Oh. Also. One of the Islands off the coast where Little A is supposed to be is called Saturna. Thinking about PtC made me think of it. But it also connects to the Greek mythology symbolism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T10:21:06-07:00","id":1512976,"title":"","content":"One of the Fun things about Supernal magic is you can specify what kind of light gets blocked. I was planning on a large scale Forces Ruling aka Control Light. Could do it a lot of ways, could lower the spectrum below the visible, could just redirect some of it. A Forces Perfecting on the starlight would be good too. I\u2019m just a bit worried someone might notice our cottage is a bit more shadowy than normal. I\u2019m sure it\u2019s possible to alleviate that, just need to think of exactly how.<br /> <br /> Beast is currently non canon to the game. It has a tendency to make people uncomfortable, and it was agreed we wouldn\u2019t use it. As it happens, I like Beast, but I will be the first to acknowledge its flaws. As for the Primordial Dream, it may still exist, since it\u2019s the realm of primal fear, but I don\u2019t think we will have a reason to go there? There are safer and easier liminal realms, like the Spire.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don\u2019t think what type of Werewolves make up most of the population in LA has come up yet. I\u2019m sure we can find out with a little investigation.<br /> <br /> As for the Factory\u2026it sounds like Infrastructure to me, but it really could be anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T10:48:02-07:00","id":1512981,"title":"","content":"I'll be interested to see, IC, how Elpis views imbuement, considering their strong commitment to the creed of &quot;Magic is Alive&quot;. Do they think of an enchantment as trapping magic or holding it captive?<br /> <br /> Also how their interpretation of &quot;Knowledge must have a price&quot; squares with Philly's interpretation of &quot;Magic is humanity's birthright.&quot; They are both young mages, so their ideas are probably still being formed and may interact and influence one another in interesting ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T11:30:09-07:00","id":1512987,"title":"","content":"OK. Help me out with this Kaiser, because you're the expert. So it seems like that maybe one way to tell the story is that the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telchines\" target=\"_blank\">Techines</a> were left-handed mages who betrayed the 'gods' (Which ones?) and fought a war with their rivals, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliadae\" target=\"_blank\">Heliadae</a>, a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mahanizrayani\" target=\"_blank\">Mahanizrayani\u200b</a> sect, who eventually won the Polema Arcane and became rulers of Rhodes. But maybe the Techines cursed the Heliadae somehow (they were masters of weather, but also poisons, killing crops, and maybe had the ability to skinchange into fish?) and that curse has been passed down through blood to Philly's mother's family.<br /> <br /> I like the Helios connection because the Sun sets over the sea near Little A. The Poseidon connection also seems like it fits with the Skywatch. It seems like Rhododendrons and Roses would be important part of the Garden (Rose hedge?)<br /> <br /> Also, maybe all this mythic glamour that is attached to the Proximi dynasties is what attracts Changelings to the area.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T11:32:45-07:00","id":1512988,"title":"","content":"Artifact wise, one that I see linking the city beyond time from Qaf's Awakening and becoming Pandora's &quot;box&quot; for Elpis is the <i>Metachronal Clock</i> (<i>Mysterium </i>page 209), with the cabal uncovering new configurations as they explore ruins, or Philly rediscovering certain Silver Ladder rituals that are needed to access new aspects of it. Guardians and Mystagogues nearby would be growing increasingly concerned as they see one layer after another being uncovered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-27-2023, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T15:09:58-07:00","id":1513005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512987#post1512987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. Help me out with this Kaiser, because you're the expert. So it seems like that maybe one way to tell the story is that the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Telchines\" target=\"_blank\">Techines</a> were left-handed mages who betrayed the 'gods' (Which ones?) and fought a war with their rivals, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heliadae\" target=\"_blank\">Heliadae</a>, a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mahanizrayani\" target=\"_blank\">Mahanizrayani\u200b</a> sect, who eventually won the Polema Arcane and became rulers of Rhodes. But maybe the Techines cursed the Heliadae somehow (they were masters of weather, but also poisons, killing crops, and maybe had the ability to skinchange into fish?) and that curse has been passed down through blood to Philly's mother's family.<br /> <br /> I like the Helios connection because the Sun sets over the sea near Little A. The Poseidon connection also seems like it fits with the Skywatch. It seems like Rhododendrons and Roses would be important part of the Garden (Rose hedge?)<br /> <br /> Also, maybe all this mythic glamour that is attached to the Proximi dynasties is what attracts Changelings to the area.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Techines betrayed the God Machine, after uncovering something at sea. The Heliadae are nebulous, some say they were backed by Helios interfering, other speak of someone seeking to use an Infrastructure to harness some kind of Divine Fire. Then I would probably throw in some elements of the Inugami manga by Hokazono to flesh out the bioorganic Mysteries that could be tied to the island and the Dynasty on Philly's mother's side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T05:23:15-07:00","id":1513063,"title":"","content":"The Metachronal Clock is an interesting idea. I once played a wizened changeling who served his durance as a book stacker in an infinite library. The <a href=\"https://avatar.fandom.com/wiki/Wan_Shi_Tong\" target=\"_blank\">keeper was quite scary!</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":". 05-28-2023, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T06:12:45-07:00","id":1513067,"title":"","content":"What if the curse is that the Proximi must live near the sea, and suffer damage, similar to the effects of drowning (including coughing up sea water) if they travel too far inland. The more knowledgeable amongst the dynasty know that not just any sea will do, but that dynasty members must live near specific &quot;islands&quot; (that are hidden to sleeper's sight). Oblation is family members bring gifts to the &quot;island&quot;, such as plants, soil, and rocks, to help prevent &quot;erosion&quot;.<br /> <br /> If this were the case, some of Philly's family might feel envious of her awakening and ability to travel to the mountains, while others, perhaps the sleeper members, feel a strong sense of unease about her straying too far from home.<br /> <br /> Blessings would be Aquaman-esque (up to three dot Transform Life: &quot;turn into a sea nymph&quot;)<br /> <br /> Or is this too corny?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T07:30:03-07:00","id":1513074,"title":"","content":"I think the baseline Curse needs to be less restrictive. It must matter, but not shut down their ability to act outside their niche. The Merovingians, for example, lose 10-again on all physical rolls and each 1 cancels a success. The Sisters of the Mountain suffer from permanent lethal damage and must sleep in soil. The Priamid can never convey the predictions they have seen and this cannot be bypassed by magic. Maybe say they must always sleep at sea, making them stand in buckets of water, sleep in a bathtub or use any other methods to carry the sea with them. That gives them a logistical challenge and a targetable weakness, but its something the cabal can normally manage.<br /> <br /> Blessings wise, they have 3 Arcana to choose from, 2 from their parent Path. 30 Arcana dots to compose the possible spell list, which are then bought like merit dots. <i>Transform Life</i> is a solid choice, so is something like <i>Speak with Animals</i>. Its all a matter of how the spells build on their theme. If you were to express the theme in one phrase, with no pauses or commas, what would it be ?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T19:57:10-07:00","id":1513154,"title":"","content":"I guess the basic idea is that they are a Ladder controlled dynasty that are both blessed and cursed by their connection to an ancestral island (I leave the exact nature of that connection to Cauthon).<br /> <br /> The &quot;bucket of water&quot; idea is interesting. Kind of like how traditionally Vampires have to carry some of their native soil around with them.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm misreading the rules, but I don't think any of this would have an effect on game play for the cabal. Awakened souls are connected to the supernal, so their Path supersedes their Proximi lineage. Philly no longer retains any blessings, nor is she cursed, and is free to go wherever she pleases. It has no mechanical effect. I suppose I could buy merit dots for it later and treat it like the allies merit or a mystery cult, but right now its just flavor for Philly's background.<br /> <br /> As to her father's family. I recently have had a quote from Balzac kicking around my head, &quot;Le secret des grandes fortunes sans cause apparente est un crime oubli\u00e9, parce qu'il a \u00e9t\u00e9 proprement fait.&quot; But again, I kind of want to leave most of that to Cauthon. I like surprises.<br /> <br /> Mysteries abound!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":"The Techines and the Heliadae) interesting. 05-28-2023, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T20:12:28-07:00","id":1513155,"title":"","content":"Oh, also &quot;Jar of dirt&quot; was a plot line in the Pirates of the Caribbean movies. But I don't remember exactly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T09:51:01-07:00","id":1513202,"title":"","content":"In the second <i>Pirates of the Caribbean</i> movie, Jack Sparrow keeps Davy Jones' heart in a jar of dirt, because Jones can only touch land for one day every 10 years. This means Jones needs to stand in buckets of seawater when on shore and that he cannot recover the heart from whoever holds it.<br /> <br /> Yep, Philly lost the benefits and downsides of her minor template when she gained the Awakened major template. Since you wanted to flesh out the details of the Dynasty, I imagined it was to make it easier if Cauthon wanted a member to show up during the chronicle. But design wise, if they could only work at full power near the shore, it would make it more difficult to drop them into a situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-29-2023, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T12:11:45-07:00","id":1513219,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Ok. That makes more sense. I don't think they would constantly need to be standing in a bucket of water though. That seems way more restrictive then saying that they mostly stay close to the ancestral island. <br /> <br /> The NPCs I have most clearly in my head right now are <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soccer_mom\" target=\"_blank\">Philly's</a> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ApronMatron\" target=\"_blank\">mother</a> (who I now picture as looking like Nichole Kidman because of the Aquaman connection, but also BIg Little Lies) and her father, the &quot;something not quite right&quot; business man. And also like a cool older cousin who is maybe a FC Moros or Acanthus (or Cauthon said there were only two FC, so maybe just FC friendly) who I think I named Kinsley IC at some point.<br /> <br /> Did Temple ever answer about Elpis and LAU, because I was also thinking about that.<br /> <br /> Lots of rain and fog where I am today. Very PNW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T12:09:25-07:00","id":1513310,"title":"","content":"Finally got around to reading the Benthic Walker Legacy. That is very interesting considering the direction Philly's mother's Proximi dynasty went. I'm not sure if Philly would ever want to pursue that Legacy, since she has a strong social component to her character* and her order affiliation, but I'm definitely interested to see what Cauthon does with it. <br /> <br /> *though it is interesting how she associates Ecstasy with isolation. And the &quot;Song&quot; was an emphasized part of her Primal Awakening. I almost considered &quot;The Song of the Deep&quot; as being part of the Proximi curse, the way Cauthon describes it as irresistible and almost addictive is very evocative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T13:12:16-07:00","id":1513315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1512981#post1512981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be interested to see, IC, how Elpis views imbuement, considering their strong commitment to the creed of &quot;Magic is Alive&quot;. Do they think of an enchantment as trapping magic or holding it captive?<br /> <br /> Also how their interpretation of &quot;Knowledge must have a price&quot; squares with Philly's interpretation of &quot;Magic is humanity's birthright.&quot; They are both young mages, so their ideas are probably still being formed and may interact and influence one another in interesting ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I've been absent, I've been sick these last few days.<br /> <br /> Elpis sees magic as a divine union between the caster's will and the symbols of the Supernal. This makes a quasi-independent entity forged from nimbus and soul, basically like a plant. It's not really sentient but still undeniably alive. They were upset by the torture spell because it both hurt someone, and it created a creature that had to hurt someone by its very existence. It didn't even have an excuse like being out of necessity like most combat spells, it only happened because someone didn't want to commit a bit of themselves to a spell or maintain it.<br /> <br /> Elpis is...bad at the &quot;Knowledge has a Price&quot; stuff. It's probably one of the main reasons they haven't made it very far in the Mysterium, along with taking their training slow. Basically, if you get them talking about a subject they like, they will talk your ear off. They mainly understand the tenet as testing if one is worthy of knowing, like the trial for summoning, and Awakening. Basically, one has to prove one can handle the power granted by knowledge. But at a certain level, they want everyone to be worthy, so they can actually have interesting conversations with peers. See the conversation with Gil about PMS. They really shouldn't have said what it stood for, but they were frazzled, and Gil had been nice, so out it went.<br /> <br /> I actually never really worked out if Elpis has gone to LAU. I mostly figured they had most of their higher education with Pandora and various other Mysterium tutors. I just didn't know the form that took.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T13:41:22-07:00","id":1513318,"title":"","content":"To actually answer your question, since I just realized I actually didn't, imbuement is like raising a plant in a greenhouse. It's a non-issue, maybe even a good thing.<br /> <br /> Of all the other factions, Elpis' ideals are most resonant with the Ladder. They just see it as the political faction, whereas they would prefer to stay out of politics and pursue Mysteries. Little do they know, academia is just as political and petty as they think politics is. Outside of being scared of Philly for being super confident with both people and spirits*, they would probably get along great.<br /> <br /> *Elpis sees Spirits as shockingly dangerous, and more than a little unnerving. Anyone who makes dealing with them their job should be respected...and maybe feared.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:43:04-07:00","id":1513328,"title":"","content":"Oh. Sorry to hear you were sick. Hope you are feeling better.<br /> <br /> I have been thinking about what the cabal dynamic will be IC, with two Obrimoi and a Thyrsus - how they view magic differently. I think Philly will strongly resonate with the idea of magic being a living, growing thing. And maybe having Thaumatugists around will help her to see the interconnectedness and emergent order of the pattern.<br /> <br /> Another potential conflict I see is whether the Ladder/Shadowwalkers or the Mysterium/Skywatch view themselves as the &quot;supervisors&quot; of the new cabal. Do Chevalier and Cloudchaser get along?<br /> <br /> I guess I was asking about LAU to gage to what degree Philly would be familiar with Elpis and Qaf when Chevalier mentions their names. It seems like there probably would not have been much interaction between the two because of the traditional jock/nerd divide and Philly's involvement in the <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/gilmoregirls/images/8/8b/Thejump.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20111219080625\" target=\"_blank\">cryptopoly/mystery cult sorority</a> at LAU. It seems likely that Philly would know Qaf though, and perhaps they were even childhood friends pre-awakening <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/revengeabc/images/e/ed/UDtSh.gif/revision/latest?cb=20170920002418\" target=\"_blank\">growing up</a> in Little A together. I kind of like the idea that Philly might view Elpis as kind of like a mystery in of themselves and be both fascinated and intimidated by their intelligence and high academic and occult skill. Philly mostly reads cheep paperback fantasies, like <a href=\"https://www.google.com/aclk?sa=l&amp;ai=DChcSEwjh_-SB_J3_AhWjBK0GHRXjB44YABADGgJwdg&amp;ase=2&amp;sig=AOD64_3vhlpptAwW6q2kebVeK_OIJK7HbA&amp;ctype=5&amp;nis=5&amp;adurl&amp;ved=2ahUKEwi7lNaB_J3_AhXzIX0KHYx4DqYQvhd6BAgBEEo\" target=\"_blank\">C.L. Moore</a>, <a href=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/91IwL1tGTeL._AC_UF1000,1000_QL80_.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Andre Norton</a> and <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1213925733i/57123.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">C.J Cherryh</a>. Maybe some <a href=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQm2jTX6p3gYDci_PnG2VGSXiDyoqsWd6UCWgBIY6oiG3-bJQJ9HZ7b1AW6Z4oMYkkMheA&amp;usqp=CAU\" target=\"_blank\">Ursula K. LeGuin</a>. And <a href=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1389418438i/41707.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Clive Cussler</a>. <br /> <br /> My mind is currently kind of blown by this whole undersea root people idea that is potentially connected to Santiago's legacy. I feel like Elpis would be interested in such entities because of their potential connection to the origins of the human soul, and for Philly they would be a fascinating spirit choir to explore.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T15:37:27-07:00","id":1513334,"title":"","content":"Well Philly is all about greenhouses (put that on the list of construction projects!) and plants. I think she probably struggles with the &quot;hunting&quot; aspect of the Primal Wild, predator and prey.<br /> <br /> I think Philly probably associates Politics with her mother, and maybe Chevalier to a certain extent, and kind of wants to get away from that. But of course she is going to get sucked back in. She really is a Silver Ladder at heart, even if she is feeling youthful rebellion.<br /> <br /> I think the way I've been playing her she is more confident on the outside than on the inside, so maybe Elpis' empathy will pick up on that. Fake it till you make it. Just don't let Philly boss Elpis around. <a href=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5a46b819a9db097eb2dd143f/1583880770026-RLPTOGBOM4BVGJACLF3D/emma-anya-taylor-joy-poster.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Ladders will do that. </a><br /> <br /> That kind of makes sense, about Elpis and spirits. Philosophically Obrimoi emphasize the <a href=\"https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/plato-parmenides/\" target=\"_blank\">one over the many</a>, so the idea that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panpsychism\" target=\"_blank\">literally everything is alive (and has a mind of its own so to speak)</a> could be frightening. I think Philly probably views Spirits somewhat naively. Most spirits do not want to be friends with humans and have very little respect for them. Long term goals. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:16:17-07:00","id":1513459,"title":"","content":"Did Temple create a backstory for Pandora before she became rapt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:25:38-07:00","id":1513460,"title":"","content":"Elpis is something of a shut in. They have a hard time making friends, and instead focus all their social energy on the few they already have. They also abuse One Mind, Two Thoughts to keep up with life while also keeping up with Mage stuff, and just generally to function, making interactions with them\u2026odd. They regularly had telepathic conversations with Pandora, and have a terrible poker face. Sometimes they just don\u2019t show up to class for a few days, and still make near perfect grades. They also have a tendency to have their head in the clouds even on a good day. They read normal novels and stuff\u2026but also books about magical theory, philosophy and mythology. Walking into walls because they were reading is not uncommon. Basically, anyone who knows of them will probably have thought of them as exceedingly eccentric, maybe spread a few rumors about them, but generally they pass under the radar.<br /> <br /> Yeah that makes sense. They tend to see that all souls are united by the Astral, basically like cells are united by the body. Even individual souls are made of cells, little aspects of emotion, memory, and reason. They have other reasons too. They at one point got ahold of a book penned by a seasoned Arrow taking about some of the more common monsters, and how to survive them. The sections on Spirits were pretty brutal, and that stuck with Elpis. The second part is they aren\u2019t sure where to place Spirits categorically on the is a person scale. Elpis like categorization. This is a rock with properties xyz, and is not a person. But Spirits blur lots of lines. They are their concept, but also not? Also Elpis is more aware than most that being able to talk with something doesn\u2019t actually make it a person. Goetia can be, but most aren\u2019t, depending on their role/archetype. See dream actors. Ghosts probably are. Spirits? They can talk and think, but can barely understand stuff outside of their related concepts. So they don\u2019t know what is appropriate to say or do around spirits, and that makes them nervous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:26:07-07:00","id":1513461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1501645#post1501645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I kept getting stuck on making the backstory for Elpis and Pandora, so I went ahead and typed up the first in-character thing. Hope it was decent, and if you have any criticisms, please feel free to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me and my dumb questions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:27:03-07:00","id":1513462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1513459#post1513459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Temple create a backstory for Pandora before she became rapt?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a bit. Mostly leaving it open for Cauthon to use for plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:31:18-07:00","id":1513463,"title":"","content":"Is it common knowledge in the consilium where the Atheneum is, or do the Mysterium keep it secret from the other orders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:35:06-07:00","id":1513464,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s a good question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:36:02-07:00","id":1513465,"title":"","content":"I guess I just noticed that Pandora wasn't listed in the Independent section of the &quot;Cast of Characters&quot; (I guess because she is dead before the story begins) so we don't know if she was part of a cabal or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:51:39-07:00","id":1513469,"title":"","content":"Mostly, I had imagined herself as an Independent with associations with the Mysterium. Preferred to wander around to investigate mysteries. Elpis doesn\u2019t know, Pandora didn\u2019t talk about her past much. A few random stories, but never anything that would place her in association with anyone specific.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s was intended that Elpis and Pandora would have formed a official cabal when Elpis was done with their apprenticeship\u2026but that didn\u2019t happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 05-31-2023, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T16:31:39-07:00","id":1513479,"title":"","content":"Qaf sees spirits as emergent properties of the grand machinery of the cosmos. Sentiment creates sentience, living ideas that compete with each other to refine themselves, implementing on what was concepted in the Astral. In that way emotions transform our reality, creating and iterating on systems dynamically.<br /> <br /> As an Arrow he knows he should not underestimate them, plus that they operate on a different train of thought than humans, but that there is enough common ground for negotiations.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are more confusing, are they the result of a memory management system ? Maybe some kind of version control ? &quot;Beats me, I am not a programmer, that is the closest parallel I could draw using what I know from sci-fi and gaming. I will just figure it out as I go, nothing beats practical experience&quot;\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T17:44:34-07:00","id":1513487,"title":"","content":"One more detail about the Cottage just came to mind. I imagine Elpis and Qaf had enough time to give it a deep cleaning, but the place has been abandoned for many years, so I imagine they still need to fumegate it, or would they have hired someone during the timeskip ? All it takes is one cast of <i>Speak with Animals</i> and anyone would be able to spy on the cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 05-31-2023, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T05:29:11-07:00","id":1513523,"title":"","content":"When Philly gets there she can do a Life ruling (Lure and Repel) spell to get rid of any harmful insects or mice. And as has already been established, life and matter provide her with many options for magical cleaning (although similar effects could be achieved with creative uses of forces or space).<br /> <br /> Although a potential area for conflict IC is what each member of the cabal considers a pest. Spiders and mice can also be friends and helpers and be given comands to guard the house. I was actually thinking the other day about how to use crows and ravens as spys and &quot;early warning system&quot; . There is also Qaf's dog as a guard option. There are also security options on the other side of the guantlet as well.<br /> <br /> Do either Elpis or Qaf have space? Because I was also thinking about how to make the cottage harder for sleepers to find. We have the mind ward still up, but maybe there is a way to make the roads to the Heights literally confusing and hard to follow. Like they get lost or driving in circles and GPS doesn't help them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T05:29:11-07:00","id":1513524,"title":"","content":"When Philly gets there she can do a Life ruling (Lure and Repel) spell to get rid of any harmful insects or mice. And as has already been established, life and matter provide her with many options for magical cleaning (although similar effects could be achieved with creative uses of forces or space).<br /> <br /> Although a potential area for conflict IC is what each member of the cabal considers a pest. Spiders and mice can also be friends and helpers and be given comands to guard the house. I was actually thinking the other day about how to use crows and ravens as spys and &quot;early warning system&quot; . There is also Qaf's dog as a guard option. There are also security options on the other side of the guantlet as well.<br /> <br /> Do either Elpis or Qaf have space? Because I was also thinking about how to make the cottage harder for sleepers to find. We have the mind ward still up, but maybe there is a way to make the roads to the Heights literally confusing and hard to follow. Like they get lost or driving in circles and GPS doesn't help them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T05:36:12-07:00","id":1513525,"title":"","content":"I guess part of my motivation for asking about cabals yesterday was the point that if there are only three major cabals than a fourth cabal, even if it is relatively small and made up of unseasoned mages, is kind of a big deal politically. So they should expect shenanigans even if they aren't attacked by overt enemies like Seers, left handed mages, or other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T06:56:05-07:00","id":1513530,"title":"","content":"I believe neither Elpis or Qaf have Space. Elpis has Mind and Qaf has Time as their extra Arcana. <br /> <br /> The animal options all depend on how skilled Philly is in securing their help. Birds, rats, spiders and ants are great informants, especially if you secure an &quot;exclusivity contract&quot;. Its one of the reasons a skilled Thyrsus is terrifying. <i>Speak with Beasts</i> is cast on the mage, rather than the animals, so one with good animal ken can have a network of discrete mundane spies, which don't trigger the Peripheral Sight and leave no Nimbus Signature (unless they are in the Long Term Nimbus' sympathetic range). So if she is discrete in her dealings, this allows her to cultivate an air of omniscience. Qaf's dog is not trained to guard, but she probably could be convinced to help. She is not a barker, so if we heard her, something is off nearby.<br /> <br /> Qaf has contacts in security firms, so he could ask them where to purchase a mundane security system with a good cost benefit, maybe Resources could be used for that ? Alternatively, Philly could make the house's interior be under <i>Machine Invisibility</i> (we don't want people to be filming a home movie and suddenly see an empty lot), but that would shut down our own security as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T11:40:25-07:00","id":1513554,"title":"","content":"You're better at creative thaumaturgy than I am, but it seems like one could have a more precise imago for Matter Veiling that would only exclude external surveillance, or be keyed to the Cabal's nimbi. Cauthon might insist on that being a higher gnosis working however. With Forces ruling you could exclude certain radio frequencies. Or if the whole cabal is comfortable with a mundane tech light set up, you could go for a localized &quot;Dresden Effect&quot; (Electronics don't work) and just run everything off a node like Elpis suggested IC. <br /> <br /> Currently Philly has Life 2 and Animal Ken 2, &quot;Speak with Beasts&quot; is her praxis, and &quot;Control instincts&quot; is one of her rotes. We will see how things go as we start taking more beats and XP. She also has Spirit 2, so she can communicate with the spirits of wildlife and plants (her long term goal is to get Spirit 4 spirit choir ranking). Her long term nimbus invokes the presence of animals, so its possible that an undiscerning observer would confuse the presence of animals with the nimbus itself.<br /> <br /> With her Life and Animal Ken skill (and Qaf's permission of course) I'm sure Qaf's dog could be trained to do all sorts of things (Mind perfecting could augment intelligence as well). What about a cat sith? With all the hedge activity it shouldn't be hard to acquire one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T11:57:00-07:00","id":1513557,"title":"","content":"Philly has <a href=\"https://youtu.be/g-r7o7Ec9uA\" target=\"_blank\">Resources 3.</a> I'm not sure how Cauthon wants me to RP that, since I've been talking about Philly's background in more of 4 or 5 dot terms. I guess the idea is that a 22 year old does not necessarily have access to all her family's funds (Like Hooper in Jaws). But three dots should be plenty for what we currently have in mind for the cottage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":". 06-01-2023, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T14:37:31-07:00","id":1513569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1513554#post1513554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're better at creative thaumaturgy than I am, but it seems like one could have a more precise imago for Matter Veiling that would only exclude external surveillance, or be keyed to the Cabal's nimbi. Cauthon might insist on that being a higher gnosis working however. With Forces ruling you could exclude certain radio frequencies. Or if the whole cabal is comfortable with a mundane tech light set up, you could go for a localized &quot;Dresden Effect&quot; (Electronics don't work) and just run everything off a node like Elpis suggested IC.<br /> <br /> Currently Philly has Life 2 and Animal Ken 2, &quot;Speak with Beasts&quot; is her praxis, and &quot;Control instincts&quot; is one of her rotes. We will see how things go as we start taking more beats and XP. She also has Spirit 2, so she can communicate with the spirits of wildlife and plants (her long term goal is to get Spirit 4 spirit choir ranking). Her long term nimbus invokes the presence of animals, so its possible that an undiscerning observer would confuse the presence of animals with the nimbus itself.<br /> <br /> With her Life and Animal Ken skill (and Qaf's permission of course) I'm sure Qaf's dog could be trained to do all sorts of things (Mind perfecting could augment intelligence as well). What about a cat sith? With all the hedge activity it shouldn't be hard to acquire one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope you mean the ones from Celtic mythology, otherwise we are doomed:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"274\" height=\"360\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://t4.ftcdn.net/jpg/05/82/94/51/360_F_582945163_jjK7mgpDRb7zLY2Gf2hveb6oatM3ntBH.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://t4.ftcdn.net/jpg/05/82/94/51/360_F_582945163_jjK7mgpDRb7zLY2Gf2hveb6oatM3ntBH.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://t4.ftcdn.net/jpg/05/82/94/51/360_F_582945163_jjK7mgpDRb7zLY2Gf2hveb6oatM3ntBH.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I am the Consilia&quot;</i><br /> <br /> If we want to make a technology curse that affects electronics without breaking them, a Shielding of Forces might be able to do it. I think we would need Fate 2 or Space 2 to apply Key-like effects. However, the Reach effect of the <i>Transmission </i>spell (core book page 144) could be used in an AoE so that only signals with our signature credentials could leave the Cottage normally.<br /> <br /> Philly has a Crafts 2, which is an incredibly flexible skill, covering fields like automotive, carpentry, jury rigging, cooking, sculpting, welding, sewing, forging, etc (CofD core book page 32). Now add a positive version of <i>Gremlins </i>(core book page 180), converting a success into an exceptional success. Since she has <i>Shaping </i>as a rote, it means that if she has the right tools, she is our crafter par excellence. <br /> <br /> Keep in mind that <i>Shaping </i>also allows her to mold the terrain to create or deny cover, cause Environmental Tilts with the Reach version, turn walls into doors, restrain opponents (sink them into the floor, trap them in walls, encase them in metal, etc), fly by standing atop an object she levitates, and much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T05:42:34-07:00","id":1513637,"title":"","content":"Is Pool a Guardian Cultor, or a Mysterium Curator? There seems to be a typo of some kind in the character description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T14:27:23-07:00","id":1513711,"title":"","content":"If I were to make an educated guess, it would be that Pool is a Mysterium Curator, based on the following ideas:<ul><li>They are a member of the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub?p=1492264#post1492264\">Kaleidoscope Keep</a>, which has a tradition of making imbued items to order, which goes against the Guardian's stance of discouraging the ample use of imbued items (<i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 75).</li> <li>They are a Forge Master, who specialize in researching and creating innovative imbued items, which is far more incentivized in the Mysterium and Free Council than the Guardians, that good relationship is reinforced by the fact that they are the Provost of a Libertine.</li> <li>It would be difficult for them to be in the Guardians, whose philosophy emphasizes self sacrifice for the greater good, when they are a crafting specialist affiliated with a Mystery Cult that refuses to make imbued weapons. Its not impossible, since there are rumors of backroom deals and people loopholing the oath, but it would be a lot of work to remain in good standing.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-02-2023, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T16:28:18-07:00","id":1513724,"title":"","content":"That is so cute! A Toy shop!<br /> <br /> Is the Keep in Little A, or is like a franchise?<br /> <br /> I'm imagining six year old Chesid (Philly) in Eitri's lap calling him Farfar while clutching her dolly or security blanket.<br /> <br /> So does that mean Dantes has a daughter? Would she be the same age as Philly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":". 06-02-2023, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T18:36:51-07:00","id":1513732,"title":"","content":"What if Keep made garden gnomes were part of our security system?<br /> &quot;It looks like its eyes keep following me...&quot;<br /> &quot;Did that one just move?&quot;<br /> &quot;I think we should leave...Oh crap!<br /> Hilarity ensues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T19:50:14-07:00","id":1513741,"title":"","content":"&quot;You must be our uninvited guests. You know, you got lucky. Another week and Philly would have finished upgrading those gnome golems to the Henderson standard.&quot;<br /> <br /> Qaf gestures for the gnomes to drag them into the Cottage.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're kind of busy right now, so we will deal with you later, throw them into the quickcarpet&quot;. They fall through the carpet, which distorts like sand, into the floor below.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Who would have guessed a weird scene from the 2000s D&amp;D movie would inspire such a good defense&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Qaf sends an audio message on Signal<br /> <br /> &quot;We got them, gnomes work great. They just fell to the basement, so they should have forgotten they entered the dream maze by now, they probably think its some hyper elaborate mage dungeon. Already asking Liberty to notify about the invasion. Don't worry, they have plenty of time to get here, I provided Elpis with copies of <i>Limbo of the Lost</i> and <i>Mystery of the Druids</i> to inspire the design, no way they are getting out in less than 24 hours. Heading back, should be there in about 30 seconds.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-02-2023, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T09:45:24-07:00","id":1513786,"title":"","content":"The <a href=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51CSD0VJHWL._AC_UF894,1000_QL80_.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Kaleidoscope Keep</a> is my new OOC obsession. I'm thinking very strongly about sinking some XP into Allies or Mystery Cult Influence merit dots for <a href=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcQ-JuW5zM3gatDDMZ_1KVN4wBRh3efxpuezA4b4uDn5xcm3fkRMt1pS62E6PSLWlU1cCMs&amp;usqp=CAU\" target=\"_blank\">Eitri</a> when I bank enough. <br /> <br /> I guess back to my original line of questioning. It seems like either Liberty or Pool has Pandora's soul Stone. Unless Watchtower or one of the other guardians kept it. If its in Guardian hands, maybe the Mysterium would look the other way or even help us if we tried to get it back. <br /> <br /> Do we know anything about Prometheus (Guardian Acanthus, no Cabal)? Would they have been connected to Pandora in some way, based on symbolic theme (Zeus is in Iron Star, and appears to be some sort of troublemaker for the Consilium).<br /> <br /> I'm just playing the political angles on Philly's behalf. Ladders gotta Ladder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T10:12:38-07:00","id":1513789,"title":"","content":"I did a search. The only reference to Pandora's soul stone's location that I could find is that IC Elpis thinks the Mysterium has it. Which again leads to the question of where the Athaneum is. If Pool is the Curator, is it dumb to think maybe its at the bottom of Tesslin's hollow? Good thing Qaf and Philly are both divers. We might need those skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":". 06-03-2023, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T11:23:50-07:00","id":1513796,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if the Athaneum is hidden, that increases pancryptia, opposite to their mission statement. The Mysterium wants you to pay for that knowledge, be it through aid, information, magic items, help researching or others. Gnostic enlightenment must be earned for it to be meaningful.<br /> <br /> They normally would outright deny you access if its too dangerous or if you can't provide quid pro quo. Guardians and Arrow help them guard the really dangerous stuff, but they are not operating under the same code.<br /> <br /> Regarding the soul stone, Qaf mentioned to Clean Sweep that Pandora's rapud desvent into Rapture is suspicious, hoping he would pass that along for Watchtower. He further mentioned the theory about a coverup. He hoped they deduced a few things he implied:<ul><li>Watchtower is a Guardian and an 11Q directly involved in the followup. They will probably frame her to both stop a competent detective from doing her job and bury whatever the Adamant Crown is really doing. All the more reason that someone besides Watchtower should be investigating it, so they can't add that to the attempts to incriminate her.</li> <li>The soul stone is a hot item, they will try to snatch it. Look how eager Ferdiad was regarding Pandora's work, it should be kept safe and warded.</li> </ul><br /> Based on that, it can't be with anyone in her cabal, because they would be accused of not being impartial. Who do we know that is a powerful Guardian, reinforced their Sanctum's defenses, was on edge and has the aid of a skilled diviner ? I think Santiago has it, it was somewhere in the lighthouse during our first visit and its why he didn't want us to use Prime Sight, so any traces of Pandora's Nimbus couldn't be spotted.<br /> <br /> Qaf has some suspicion, but I think Elpis has a higher chance to make that deduction, since they were the only ones who saw him on guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-03-2023, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T12:28:26-07:00","id":1513802,"title":"","content":"I agree about further investigation into the potential cover-up of Pandora's presumed death. Based on what you say about the Mysterium's principle of &quot;Knowledge must have a price&quot;, it is possible that they may be willing to trade the Stone for the Grimoire that Elpis and Qaf found in the cottage after the cabal is done with their own investigation (assuming the Stone is more valuable for our purposes than whatever mystery is hidden in the Grimoire), along with any other knowledge we may uncover about the Corenne and the Cottage (it is even possible that there is a connection between the mystery of the cottage and Pandora's enrapture). But, like you say, no legitimate acquisition of the stone is likely until the circumstances of Pandora's decline and death are cleared up. Also, all the more reason to increase security of the Cottage if the cabal wants to lay claim to it without a fight.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of conflicting loyalties here, especially bringing Philly, a moderately notable and well connected Ladder, into the situation. If it is the case that Qaf and Philly know one another, or have been friends since before both of their awakenings, there may be a degree of trust. But there also may not be. I think Philly will probably be suspicious of Chevalier's motivations in sending her into the middle of this thing. But it's also a big step up from low level cryptopoly assignments and sorority parties *, so Philly may feel like she has to prove herself - that she is not a &quot;kid&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> If you are correct and the stone is in the Lighthouse, I assume that it is impregnable especially with our current abilities (Every time she peers across the gauntlet Philly is probably like <a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/lotr/images/b/b8/Alan_Lee_-_Orthanc.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20140526033440\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;What the ...?</a>&quot;. So we may need to do a &quot;favor&quot; for Santiago to get what we want (assuming that regaining the soul stone is one of our main goals).<br /> <br /> I guess I just thought the shadow name Pool was very suggestive given the presence of a mysterious quarry lake near by. Who knows?<br /> <br /> Lots of stuff to do. Mysteries abound.<br /> <br /> *I've been thinking of the LAIU sorority in cryptopoly/mystery cult terms. Not sure if Cauthon wants me to work on that or keep it behind the ST screen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T12:49:18-07:00","id":1513806,"title":"","content":"I think the end of the conversation with Clean Sweep was to check where Elpis and Qaf's loyalties lie. Elpis has stated they are wary of how they join the Elan, but they have an Obsession with this Mystery. Simultaneously, he was checking if Qaf seems aligned with the Adamant Crown's ideals.<br /> <br /> I think Chevalier (same Order and Legacy as Clean Sweep) might be sending Philly in to keep an ear to the ground. Same Order as them, family ties to Chevalier, new mage so it won't be suspicious. So if anything hits these wild cards, it will be natural for them to know.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T16:00:43-07:00","id":1513823,"title":"","content":"Wild Cards!?<br /> <br /> I have been thinking about cabal theme/shadow name.<br /> <br /> Three is kind of a weird number in terms of the game: fours, fives, and tens are more typical. But there are lots of spiritual/mythological connections to three.<br /> <br /> Qafsiel is traditionally one of three angels guarding the seventh heaven (the sphere of Saturn). Philophrosyne is one the Charities (or Graces). There are usually three of those. I chose the name because of its connection to Hephaestus (the god of crafting), but also the nimbus it invokes (Hospitality, Generosity, Joy, Kindness, Good Times). There is also a possible mythic connection to Nyx and Pandora.<br /> <br /> I was also thinking the other day about how the three characters relate to the three theological virtues:<br /> Faith - Qafsiel has a message from the oracle/gods of Aether, but also fidelity and oath keeping are very important to Arrows.<br /> Hope - Elpis<br /> Love - Philia is the love between friends.<br /> <br /> Or it could be Chesed (Philly's sympathetic name), Gevurah, and Tiferet - the three primary emotions of Ein Sof in Kabbalah. <br /> <br /> What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T16:57:51-07:00","id":1513829,"title":"","content":"I think I finally found an image that could be used as a basis of the cabal's emblem:<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"375\" height=\"580\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/54243095e4b07ee637a9f812/93f93257-6109-4341-91ff-63f7d350654a/the-world-tarotF.jpg?format=750w\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/54243095e4b07ee637a9f812/93f93257-6109-4341-91ff-63f7d350654a/the-world-tarotF.jpg?format=750w\" data-thumb-url=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/54243095e4b07ee637a9f812/93f93257-6109-4341-91ff-63f7d350654a/the-world-tarotF.jpg?format=750w\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> <br /> We have the stars for Elpis, the Tree of Life for Philly, the divine light for Qaf, brought together into the full glory of <a href=\"https://www.angelarium.net/treeoflife#/ein-sof/\" target=\"_blank\">the tree of Ein Sof</a> to represent the cabal. What do you all think ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-03-2023, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T18:23:51-07:00","id":1513835,"title":"","content":"I'm sold!!! Tikkun Olam!<br /> <br /> What do you think Temple?<br /> <br /> Also if the whole Elan thing doesn't work out for Elpis, the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Eyes_of_Ain_Soph\" target=\"_blank\">Seekers</a> are always recruiting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T18:42:57-07:00","id":1513836,"title":"","content":"I like Faith, Hope and Love. Though I admit, I normally associate Qaf with prudence. And that drawing is amazing. Yeah. I\u2019m happy with that.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Seekers have a branch focused on Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T18:44:25-07:00","id":1513837,"title":"","content":"On a more somber note, uh <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27258_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27258\" data-vbnamecard=\"27258\">Cauthon</a>? Are you doing ok? Haven\u2019t heard from you in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T18:56:39-07:00","id":1513838,"title":"","content":"It's a 1E Legacy and I don't think there's been an official update, so I'm sure you could run with it however you want. They explore magical traditions, so what better way to do that than in the Temenos? Or you could talk to stars in the Anima Mundi.<br /> <br /> Yeah, me too. Hope they're OK.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":". 06-03-2023, 10:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T19:36:22-07:00","id":1513840,"title":"","content":"Looks like all the spirit options for attainments could equally apply to Goetia. But Cauthon and Kaiser are the legacy experts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-03T20:26:50-07:00","id":1513842,"title":"","content":"Hope Cauthon is doing ok, maybe its been a pretty hectic week and he is exhausted.<br /> <br /> There is a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1106424#post1106424\">conversion to 2ed</a>. They are from the Mysterium, its parent Path is Obrimos, but its Ruling Arcanum is Prime and the optional is Spirit. Another option, which I think would synergize well with Elpis' theme of Hope, would be the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1405749-new-legacy-oneiric-physicians\">Oneiric Physicians</a>. Mind primary and Prime secondary, they could be the result of meeting the Bellerophon Group and learning more about the mechanics of Rapture, seeking to increase the odds of people recovering from it. They also seek to increase people's mental wellness and open Sleeper's minds to the possibility of Awakening, igniting a torch of hope in the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-03-2023, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T03:05:07-07:00","id":1513998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CalvinSiler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/1501180-in-the-hallowed-light-mtaw2e-ooc?p=1513637#post1513637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Pool a Guardian Cultor, or a Mysterium Curator? There seems to be a typo of some kind in the character description.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was probably a transcription error - I had to shuffle a bunch of people when I repurposed my Prohibition-era Consilium. Removing two whole Cabals kinda futzed with things. She's a Mysterium Curator.<br /> <br /> As for the Athenaeum, it's known to be in an extradimensional pocket of some kind (Space? Spirit? Death? WHO KNOWS!), but the actual location is unknown to outsiders and Neokoros. Pool keeps a catalog of current contents, and brings out items to approved personnel.<br /> <br /> The Keep is... kinda a franchise? The subsidiaries don't tend to overlap, and the individual journeymen are fairly spread out. Eitri lives in Stockholm, but his Workshop subsidiary of the Keep has a member in Vancouver (Just a hop skip and a jump away!). Pool is a member of the Cogwork Consortium, the clock makers and wind-up toy-makers<br /> <br /> The Mysterium alledgedly has Pandora's Soulstone. Likely stored under heavy Warding in the Athenaeum.<br /> <br /> I'm sure I missed some questions, gimme a heads up on anything you spot.<br /> <br /> Sorry I've been gone so long - finished my mom's visit and should be good to go now. I'll get working on the IC posts","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-06-2023, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T06:13:08-07:00","id":1514006,"title":"","content":"No worries. Glad you got to spend time with your mom!<br /> <br /> I think we settled on a Kabbalah-esque theme for the cabal (Angels, Tree of Life, Stars, &quot;Repair the World&quot;, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T08:12:24-07:00","id":1514014,"title":"","content":"Yep, family always comes first, hope you had an awesome visit !<br /> <br /> I wonder what Chevalier did, if she didn't cast a spell, maybe she used a Fetish ? An Attainment ? She is a Keeper of the Covenant, so maybe not. If that is how Philly remembers the cottage, I can't help but imagine her younger self thinking the Adams Family lived there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T10:45:40-07:00","id":1514022,"title":"","content":"How about <i>The Korsian Stellarium</i> ? We have <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beri%27ah\" target=\"_blank\">Korsia</a> symbolically associated with the theme of heart, the dwelling of archangels, the soul garment of thought and a direct connection to the Tree of Life. Stellarium ties into Elpis's star symbolism and also into the Ptolomeic model of the cosmos, which is associated with the Heavenly Spheres by Dante's <i>Paradiso</i>.<br /> <br /> The main worry is if its clear that the world Korsia is meant to align with Supernal order, or the The Star-Cloaked King of Thunder at best, rather than <b>The Throne</b>.<br /> <br /> But anyway, how does that name sound ?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-06-2023, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2647"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:03:53-07:00","id":1514024,"title":"","content":"Lol. Things always look bigger when you're little. <br /> <br /> Well her dad's family is Moros path. So they probably have Adams vibes.<br /> <br /> I think it's interesting playing around with a character who's been exposed to magic since childhood. I imagine most proximi need therapy. Especially a Ladder controlled family.<br /> <br /> That last post did get me thinking about what an ill intentioned warlock could do with Philly's sympathetic name. She seems kind of sniffy about the Guardians, even though they've probably been protecting her her whole life. <br /> <br /> But look at me giving the ST ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:10:21-07:00","id":1514026,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking about the workshop and &quot;heirloom dolls&quot;. Maybe Philly learned about <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=nTB3ZRz50dg\" target=\"_blank\">magath</a> the hard way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T11:24:02-07:00","id":1514027,"title":"","content":"The &quot;world of formation&quot; also kind of sounds like the astral realm, especially if you use the teacher and the lesson analogy. And it definitely sounds like we might spend sometime there even though it gives the Thyrsus in the cabal the Willie's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":"&qu 06-06-2023, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T13:21:28-07:00","id":1514045,"title":"","content":"Oh, Chevalier's just got a gaggle of Spirits with her. They do little things like open doors, temperature control, and open Doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T14:19:16-07:00","id":1514048,"title":"","content":"Wait. Was I being thick? I guess I just assumed Chevalier was using mind. But then I caught the &quot; Amore&quot; reference. Is this something Philly would be ...familiar with? Or what would I see with Active mage sight?<br /> <br /> Sorry I was jumping the gun. Too eager I guess.<br /> <br /> Edit: also, was I being too informal before? How do you want to handle social maneuvering going forward? Since Philly is a more socially oriented character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","user":"CalvinSiler","date":". 06-06-2023, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T14:34:32-07:00","id":1514053,"title":"","content":"You weren't being thick, it's just intentionally vague. Peripheral Mage Sight would only ping on a Spirit if they're actively using one of their powers, so the only cue you had for it was me changing the name's color.<br /> <br /> Spirit Mage Sight (as long as you have two Dots of Spirit) would let you see Spirits in Twilight. Or if you have <u>Exorcist\u2019s Eye</u> cast. Philly is probably used to Chevalier's attendants doing little things, but not them futzing with people's minds. She's <i>aware</i> that Spirits can do that though.<br /> <br /> You didnt jump the gun, and you werent too informal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 06-06-2023, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T14:53:42-07:00","id":1514055,"title":"","content":"Ok. I can edit the post to reflect that. Yeah Philly probably has views on using spirits that way. She is still young (and Wisdom 7). <br /> <br /> She does have 2 dots or I can cast exorists eye if you want. Do you want to describe what she saw?<br /> <br /> While I was posting I kept feeling like I was missing something. You described a spirit &quot;nudge&quot; very well with the waiter's facial expression change. Now I'm curious about the &quot;portal&quot; effect you used to get us to the Rose, because I assumed that was space. Philly clearly has lots of things to learn from her mentor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T15:23:28-07:00","id":1514058,"title":"","content":"I have a guess on that one. <i>Co-Location</i> with 1 Reach for instant use, one for sensory range, one for creating a portal, plus a mana for sympathetic range and a combined <i>Scry </i>so you could see the destination for extra style points. She probably sent a familiar ahead to verify when she could teleport in, the used her Connected sympathy to teleport seemingly without setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/